egin first small-batch commercial shipments to Chinese customers of its China-tailored, modified LPU chip developed using licensed Groq technology by December 31, 2026, as confirmed by NVIDIA's results disclosures or commercial shipment confirmations?\n   154\tA: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2026-12-31.\n   155\tReason: The reference is The Information's reported plan for small-batch shipments by year-end, with Chinese firms said to have placed orders; that expectation sits at rung 1. I forecast that the specified China-tailored chip will not have qualifying shipment confirmation by December 31: the reported target is specific, but remains a report of intent, while NVIDIA excludes China Data Center compute revenue from its outlook and said it could not then deliver a competitive product for wide distribution with both US and Chinese approval. NVIDIA's full-production announcement concerns Groq 3 LPX on the Vera Rubin platform, not confirmation of shipments of the China-tailored variant. No formal abandonment or Chinese prohibition after August 20 is shown, so rung 2 is not the forecast either. The newly reported acceleration of Huawei's chip schedule adds competition context but does not establish an alternative outcome for this chip by the deadline.\n   156\t- round-0/claude: supported | This is NVIDIA's reported vehicle for re-entering China data-centre inference, with orders placed, a material revenue bet distinct from H200 imports. A rumoured plan against NVIDIA's zero-China guidance and stated approval barriers justifies 'still open'.\n   157\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | Re-entry into China’s large AI-compute market could materially affect NVIDIA. The specific shipment plan, reported orders and compliant hardware favor rung 1; guidance and restrictions on wide distribution do not sufficiently outweigh them for small-batch shipments by year-end.\n   158\t- round-1/claude: supported | Rung 1 rests on one anonymous report of intent. NVIDIA guides zero China data-centre revenue and cites both-government approval barriers, Beijing approval is unresolved, and NVIDIA confirmation is needed by year-end, so rung 3 is defensible.\n   159\t- round-1/codex: unsupported | China re-entry could materially affect NVIDIA. The reported year-end plan, orders and compliant hardware favor shipments. Zero-China guidance and barriers to wide distribution do not sufficiently outweigh that specific evidence for small-batch shipments.\n   160\t- round-2/claude: supported | Rung 1 rests on one secondhand report of intent that needs Beijing approval and NVIDIA confirmation. Zero-China guidance, stated dual-approval barriers and unresolved Chinese import permissions make rung 3 a reasonable forecast, consistent with its reasons.\n   161\t- round-2/codex: unsupported | China re-entry could materially affect NVIDIA. The specific year-end shipment plan, reported orders and compliant hardware favor rung 1. Zero-China guidance and obstacles to wide distribution do not sufficiently outweigh that evidence for a small-batch launch.\n   162\t\n   163\t### 17. new-3 Q26 (C003) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   164\tQ: What cumulative amount, in USD, has NVIDIA paid or committed under the Poolside Model Factory licence and associated equity investment, Groq arrangement and Enfabrica arrangement as of FY2027 year-end, counting paid amounts only once, as disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K and intervening Form 10-Q filings?\n   165\tA: from 20,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD\n   166\tReason: The reference is NVIDIA's reported aggregate of roughly $27bn, which sits in rung 3. The evidence implies about $24.9bn: Poolside's $6bn licence plus $1bn investment, Groq's $13bn closing consideration plus $4bn payable, and about $0.9bn for Enfabrica. The Groq cash outflow and accrued consideration are payment details within that arrangement, not additional amounts; the $2.5bn intangible asset is not additional consideration. The implied total remains below the $25bn rung-3 boundary.\n   167\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | About $27bn of licence-and-hire outlays is cash-material. Rung 2 rests on $24.9bn, $0.1bn below the boundary using an approximate Enfabrica figure. It ignores the unexplained ~$3bn gap to Groq's $20bn and August Groq investment.\n   168\t- round-0/codex: supported | The roughly $25 billion commitment is material, and no earlier question tracks the same outcome. The reported components imply about $24.9 billion without double counting; that supports rung 2, although the estimate is close to the boundary.\n   169\t- round-1/claude: unsupported | The $24.9bn sum sits $0.1bn under the boundary and relies on an approximate Enfabrica figure. The ~$3bn gap to Groq's $20bn and the August Groq investment push upward, toward the rung-3 $27bn reference.\n   170\t- round-1/codex: unsupported | The deals are material and distinct from earlier questions. The $24.9bn estimate relies on an approximate Enfabrica figure just below the boundary and does not reconcile Groq’s $17bn disclosed consideration with its reported $20bn value.\n   171\t\n   172\t### 18. new-3 Q31 (C113) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   173\tQ: By NVIDIA's FY2027 year-end on January 31, 2027, will China's antitrust regulators have issued a formal decision concluding the investigation into NVIDIA's compliance with its Mellanox acquisition conditions, following the September 15, 2025 preliminary finding, as documented in a regulator announcement or NVIDIA 10-Q/10-K disclosure published by that date?\n   174\tA: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\n   175\tReason: The reference is the disclosed regulatory status: a preliminary finding, with no stated deadline for a final decision. That sits at rung 3, Still open. The filing still describes only that preliminary finding and possible consequences if regulators reach a conclusion; it supplies no indication that a decision or formal withdrawal is scheduled by January 31, 2027. Continued openness is therefore the most likely outcome, though not established as fact.\n   176\t- round-0/claude: supported | A SAMR ruling could bring penalties or restrictions on NVIDIA's China networking business, a material risk, and no earlier question covers it. The filing shows only a year-old preliminary finding with no timetable, so 'still open' fits.\n   177\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Potential penalties or networking restrictions could materially affect NVIDIA, and no earlier question tracks this investigation. The preliminary finding establishes an open case, but no timing evidence supports choosing continued openness over a decision by the deadline.\n   178\t- round-1/claude: supported | The August 2026 filing still shows only the year-old preliminary finding, with no timetable. A year without a ruling and five months left make 'still open' the reasoned default over a decision, so the material is not too thin.\n   179\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Potential penalties or networking restrictions make the investigation material, and no earlier question tracks it. The preliminary finding establishes an open case, but the absence of a timetable does not justify preferring continued openness over a decision by the deadline.\n   180\t- round-2/claude: supported | The August 2026 filing still reports only the September 2025 preliminary finding, with no timetable. Eleven months without a ruling and five months left make 'still open' the reasoned default. The material is thin but still chooses an answer.\n   181\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Potential penalties or networking restrictions make the case material, and no earlier question tracks the same outcome. The year-old preliminary finding and lack of a timetable do not establish whether continued openness or a decision by January is more likely.\n   182\t\n   183\t### 19. new-3 Q39 (C196) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   184\tQ: Will the US Department of Justice publish a decision or conclusion on its antitrust review of NVIDIA's $20 billion Groq licensing/acqui-hire arrangement by January 31, 2027, as established by DOJ public statements, court filings, a consent decree, confirmation of closure, or NVIDIA's periodic filings?\n   185\tA: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\n   186\tReason: The available reference is a reported active DOJ review with no public resolution timetable, which sits at rung 3, Still open. The reported formal information request and possible negotiated conditions make a public conclusion possible, but neither supplies a concrete decision step or timing that makes a conclusion by January 31, 2027 more likely than the review remaining open. Rung 2 is unsupported: there is no evidence of a formal abandonment or withdrawal after September 10, 2026.\n   187\t- round-0/claude: supported | A DOJ challenge, unwind or consent decree on a $20B arrangement is material and distinct from the financing-arrangements question. The material shows an active review with a fresh information request and no timetable, so 'still open' is justified.\n   188\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | The DOJ review concerns a major NVIDIA transaction and is distinct from earlier questions. An ongoing inquiry without a resolution timetable does not establish whether it is more likely to remain open or conclude by January 31.\n   189\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported. A newly reported formal information request, no timetable, and DOJ's habit of rarely announcing closures make 'still open' the reasoned default. The material is enough to prefer rung 3; nothing points to a conclusion or abandonment.\n   190\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | The review concerns a major transaction and is distinct from earlier questions. An active inquiry without a resolution timetable does not establish whether it is more likely to conclude or remain open by January 31.\n   191\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. The review is active, a formal information request was only recently reported, and no timetable exists. Investigations at that stage rarely resolve within four months, so the material justifies rung 3 over rung 1. Nothing suggests abandonment.\n   192\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The major Groq arrangement warrants tracking and is distinct from earlier questions. The reported inquiry and information request establish no resolution timetable; the material does not justify preferring continued openness over a public conclusion by January 31.\n   193\t\n   194\t### 20. new-3 Q4 (C167) answer-mark=unsupported type=yes/no\n   195\tQ: Will Nvidia's Kyber-based Vera Rubin Ultra systems reach first commercial shipments by December 31, 2027, as confirmed by Nvidia's results or shipment announcements, or customer deployment confirmations?\n   196\tA: After July 5, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels Kyber-based Vera Rubin Ultra systems or decides to defer all first commercial shipments beyond December 31, 2027. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\n   197\tReason: The reference is NVIDIA's stated 2027 timeline, which sits at rung 1. The more specific forecast for the Kyber NVL144 rack is SemiAnalysis's report that it has slipped by more than a year, from 2027 to 2028; if that schedule stands, it implies a post-2026-07-05 decision to defer first Kyber shipments beyond the deadline, the rung-2 outcome. NVIDIA's statements that its roadmap is intact and that Vera Rubin is in production are counterevidence, but do not specifically establish Kyber shipments or an unchanged Kyber schedule. The new reports of Vera Rubin racks running at partners are meaningful platform progress, not confirmation of commercial shipments of Kyber-based Rubin Ultra systems. The evidence therefore still makes a standing deferral more likely than shipments by the deadline, while not establishing that deferral as fact.\n   198\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | Kyber Rubin Ultra timing is a major revenue bet; no earlier card covers it. Rung 2 requires a formal post-July-5 Nvidia deferral, but SemiAnalysis's slip predates July 5 and Nvidia repeatedly reaffirms 2027. Evidence points to rung 1 or 3.\n   199\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | Kyber’s shipment timing is material and distinct from the earlier Vera Rubin question. The reported delay predates or coincides with opening, so it does not justify forecasting the post-July 5 decision required for rung 2.\n   200\t\n   201\t### 21. new-3 Q40 (C025) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=figure\n   202\tQ: How many GW of combined new AI factory capacity will NVIDIA's eight Australian DSX partners—Firmus, Sharon AI, IREN, Megaport, ResetData, CDC, NEXTDC and AirTrunk—have brought online in Australia by 31 December 2027, as established by their capacity disclosures and Data Centres Australia's capacity statistics?\n   203\tA: from 0.5 GW to below 1.8 GW\n   204\tReason: The reference is NVIDIA's target of up to 2GW by 2027, which sits in rung 3 (1.8GW to below 2.2GW). The evidence supports a forecast of about 0.9GW, not the full target: I credit the 42MW Firmus facility and some, but not all, of CDC's 800MW under construction and IREN's disclosed development. IREN's 480MW AI Cloud goal by end-2026 adds a more specific nearer-term signal, but its Australian share and overlap with Bundey are unclear. CDC's figures cover Australia and New Zealand and are not all identified as DSX capacity; the Bundey figure is a campus plan, not a confirmed amount online by the deadline. Sharon AI's GPU target has no stated installation timetable or capacity share. The resulting estimate remains below the 1.8GW boundary for rung 3.\n   205\t- round-0/claude: supported | A 2GW, roughly $80B Australian buildout is big enough to move NVIDIA revenue. The 'up to' target, partial CDC/IREN pipelines, ANZ-wide figures and no schedules make the wide 0.5–1.8GW rung a reasonable pick over 1.8GW+.\n   206\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | A potential 2 GW buildout is material to NVIDIA. But the disclosures do not establish enough Australian DSX capacity or delivery timing to justify a forecast above 0.5 GW over the lower range.\n   207\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported. CDC's 800MW under construction, IREN's 480MW-by-2026 goal and Bundey, Firmus's 42MW, and the 2GW 'up to' target make 0.5–1.8GW more likely than below 0.5GW. Missing schedules justify discounting below 1.8GW.\n   208\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | The potential buildout is material to NVIDIA. But the target and unscheduled, partly non-Australian development figures do not justify choosing 0.5–1.8 GW over below 0.5 GW; the 0.9 GW estimate lacks a supported capacity breakdown.\n   209\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. CDC's 800MW under construction, Sharon AI's 68,000 GPUs, Firmus's funded Southgate and eight large operators building over 15 months make the wide 0.5–1.8GW band likelier than below 0.5GW. Missing schedules justify staying below 1.8GW.\n   210\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The potential buildout is material to NVIDIA. The 2 GW target and partly non-Australian, unscheduled project figures do not establish enough qualifying capacity to favor 0.5–1.8 GW over below 0.5 GW; the 0.9 GW forecast lacks a substantiated breakdown.\n   211\t\n   212\t### 22. new-3 Q9 (C002) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=figure\n   213\tQ: What total amount of dark-fiber/telecom network capital and purchase/capacity commitments for NVIDIA's US GPU-as-a-Service and dark-fiber build-out will NVIDIA disclose as of FY2027 year-end in its FY2027 annual report, supplemented by its quarterly commitment disclosures?\n   214\tA: below 2,500,000,000 USD\n   215\tReason: The reference is Needham's estimated $5–10 billion cost over three years, which sits in rung 3. That is an estimate of project cost, not a quantified NVIDIA disclosure of the requested capital or purchase/capacity commitments. The new and repeated Zayo reports make the fiber build more concrete, but disclose no NVIDIA commitment amount; the multi-year optics agreements and Corning facilities partnership likewise provide no attributable dollar amount. I therefore still forecast less than $2.5 billion specifically disclosed for this build-out by FY2027 year-end. The $119 billion total supply-commitment figure is not broken out for these agreements, so it cannot be counted toward this question.\n   216\t- round-0/claude: supported | A $5–10B telecom/dark-fiber build is a distinct bet on cash and capex. It is not the total-commitments question. No item quantifies an NVIDIA commitment, and the $119B total is not broken out, so a specific disclosure below $2.5B is reasonable.\n   217\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | The reported $5–10 billion project could be financially material, and its network-specific commitments can differ from total supply commitments. No evidence sizes NVIDIA’s attributable disclosure or supports the below-$2.5 billion forecast over other ranges.\n   218\t- round-1/claude: supported | The question resolves on what NVIDIA discloses, not on project cost. Every item shows no broken-out NVIDIA amount: Zayo, optics and Corning give no terms, and $119B is aggregate. So disclosure below $2.5B, rung 1, is the reasoned default.\n   219\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | The network project could be financially material and is distinct from total supply commitments. The $5–10 billion estimate does not size NVIDIA’s attributable FY2027 disclosure, and the absence of disclosed amounts does not favor below $2.5 billion over other ranges.\n   220\t- round-2/claude: supported | The question resolves on NVIDIA's separately disclosed amount, not project cost. The material shows NVIDIA reporting only an aggregate $119B and unpriced Zayo, optics and Corning deals, so rung 1 is the reasoned forecast.\n   221\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The project could be material and is distinct from total supply commitments. The evidence does not size NVIDIA’s attributable commitments or indicate what it will disclose by year-end, so it does not favor below $2.5 billion over the other ranges.\n   222\t\n   223\t### 23. old-1 Q16 (C098) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   224\tQ: Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by December 31, 2026?\n   225\tA: The Senate has not passed RASA by December 31, 2026.\n   226\tReason: No market consensus is supplied. The deadline reference is passage by December 31, 2026 (rung 1); the alternative is that the Senate has not passed RASA by then (rung 2). RASA had passed the House but was still awaiting Senate action on July 23, and the August 19 report says it had still not passed. With about four months remaining and no stated Senate timetable or movement, the evidence favors no passage by the deadline. Reports of remote chip access and the gap in existing controls increase the policy case for action, but do not indicate that the Senate is moving toward a vote, so they do not overcome the stalled status.\n   227\t- round-0/claude: supported | RASA would extend export controls to cloud access to NVIDIA chips, a regulatory bet that could change China-linked revenue; no earlier card covers it. Bill stalled in Senate as of August 19 with no timetable, supporting no passage.\n   228\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Remote-access export controls could materially affect demand for NVIDIA’s advanced chips. But a bill awaiting Senate action, without evidence about its prospects or timetable, is too thin a basis to favor either deadline outcome.\n   229\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported: a House-passed bill still stalled in the Senate seven months later, with no timetable or scheduled vote and four months left, justifies the status-quo answer. Most such bills never pass, so the material is not too thin.\n   230\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Remote-access export controls could materially affect demand for NVIDIA chips. The bill’s pending status and absence of a reported timetable do not establish whether passage or nonpassage by year-end is more likely.\n   231\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported: the material shows the bill stalled in the Senate from January to August 19, with no scheduled vote. With four months left, that justifies the default no-passage answer, and the reasons follow the material.\n   232\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Remote-access controls could materially affect NVIDIA’s chip demand. The bill’s pending status and lack of a reported Senate timetable do not establish whether passage or nonpassage by year-end is more likely.\n   233\t\n   234\t### 24. old-1 Q20 (C175) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   235\tQ: Will NVIDIA agree to finance OpenAI chip purchases for the southern Ohio data center project by January 31, 2027?\n   236\tA: NVIDIA has not agreed to finance OpenAI chip purchases for the project by 2027-01-31.\n   237\tReason: The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus, NVIDIA guidance, or stated plan says NVIDIA will agree to finance OpenAI’s chip purchases by January 31, 2027. The specific reports and NVIDIA’s statement establish discussions of up to $350 billion in GPU financing, but discussions are not an agreement. NVIDIA’s disclosed commitments are instead guarantees for land, power, and shell buildout, and the reported vendor-financing denial weighs against those discussions becoming a chip-purchase financing commitment by the deadline. The evidence therefore leaves No more likely than Yes and does not cross the rung boundary.\n   238\t- round-0/claude: supported | Financing up to $350B of OpenAI GPU purchases could change NVIDIA's revenue and credit risk; the earlier guarantee question is a separate bet. Only preliminary talks are reported, while signed commitments cover land, power and shell, so No holds.\n   239\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Potential chip financing of up to $350 billion is material and distinct from the earlier facility guarantee. Talks establish a possibility, but the evidence gives too little basis to judge whether agreement by the deadline is more likely than not.\n   240\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported. Talks were confirmed but stayed preliminary as of mid-August. The signed filing covers only land, power and shell, and NVIDIA denied vendor financing. That is enough to choose No over Yes, so the material is not too thin.\n   241\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Potential chip financing is material and distinct from the facility guarantee. Preliminary talks and a general denial of vendor financing do not provide enough evidence to judge whether an agreement by the deadline is more likely than not.\n   242\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. Talks were confirmed but preliminary and could collapse. The August filing committed only land/power/shell guarantees, with no chip financing, and NVIDIA denied vendor financing. With no agreement and four months left, No over Yes is justified.\n   243\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The potential financing is material and distinct from the facility guarantee. Preliminary talks and a denial of current vendor financing do not establish whether an agreement by January is more or less likely than not.\n   244\t\n   245\t### 25. old-1 Q22 (C057) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   246\tQ: Will Taiwan’s Ministry of Economic Affairs adopt performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027?\n   247\tA: No competent Taiwanese authority formally adopts performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027.\n   248\tReason: The reference is rung 2: no formal adoption by the deadline is indicated in the available plan or timeline. The consultations and reported consideration make adoption more plausible than before, but the Ministry set no timeline; that evidence does not make formal adoption by January 31, 2027 the more likely outcome. The forecast therefore remains below the rung-1 boundary.\n   249\t- round-0/claude: supported | Taiwan fabs and assembles nearly all NVIDIA chips, so its own export controls could hit China sales and supply-chain licensing. The only material is consultations with no timeline, which supports no formal adoption within six months.\n   250\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Taiwanese advanced-chip export controls could materially affect NVIDIA’s supply chain and sales. Consultations and reported consideration establish possibility, but no timeline or other evidence establishes whether adoption by the deadline is more or less likely than not.\n   251\t- round-1/claude: supported | Only consultations and reported consideration, with no draft rule and explicitly no timeline. Formal adoption within six months is therefore not indicated, so the material reasonably favours no adoption by the deadline over its neighbour.\n   252\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Taiwanese advanced-chip controls could materially affect NVIDIA’s supply chain and sales. Consultations and reported consideration establish a possibility of adoption, but the absence of a timeline alone does not establish which outcome is more likely by the deadline.\n   253\t- round-2/claude: supported | Binary with no adoption as the status quo. The material shows only consultations and reported weighing, with no draft and explicitly no timeline. That reasonably favours no formal adoption within six months; it is not too thin to choose.\n   254\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Taiwanese advanced-chip export controls could materially affect NVIDIA. Consultations and reported consideration establish a possibility of adoption, but no timeline or evidence about the adoption process is provided to justify choosing either outcome as more likely by the deadline.\n   255\t\n   256\t### 26. old-1 Q26 (C065) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   257\tQ: Will Taiwan adopt a criminal ban on all AI chip exports to China by January 31, 2027?\n   258\tA: Taiwan has not adopted a criminal ban on all AI chip exports to China by January 31, 2027.\n   259\tReason: The reference is rung 1: the supplied evidence says Taiwan is considering a ban, not that it has adopted one. That consideration, in the context of an investigation into suspected smuggling, raises the prospect of action, but the evidence gives no adopted measure, legislative stage, or timetable. The most likely outcome by January 31, 2027 therefore remains no adoption; the evidence does not shift the forecast across the rung boundary.\n   260\t- round-0/claude: supported | A Taiwanese criminal ban could block NVIDIA's China shipments routed through Taiwan, including any H200 sales, so it can move revenue. It differs from the earlier performance-threshold question. The material shows only consideration, with no adopted measure or timetable.\n   261\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | A broad export ban could materially affect NVIDIA, and it differs from performance-threshold controls. Mere consideration of a ban, without evidence on its prospects or timetable, is too thin to establish the more likely outcome by January.\n   262\t- round-1/claude: supported | The material shows only that Taiwan is considering a ban, with no bill, legislative stage or timetable. Criminal legislation rarely passes within four months, so the status quo of no adoption is justified over its neighbour.\n   263\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | A broad ban could materially affect NVIDIA and is distinct from performance-threshold controls. Consideration alone, without evidence about adoption prospects or timing, is too thin to choose the more likely outcome by January.\n   264\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. The material shows only consideration, with no bill, legislative stage or timetable. With about four months left, no adoption is the evidence-consistent default. The reasons match the material, and nothing points toward adoption.\n   265\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | A broad ban could materially affect NVIDIA and is distinct from threshold controls. Consideration alone provides too little evidence to favor either adoption outcome by January; the claimed legislative base rate is not supplied.\n   266\t\n   267\t### 27. old-1 Q27 (C145) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   268\tQ: Will the U.S. Department of Commerce conclude its investigation into Chinese firms’ access to advanced U.S. chips by December 31, 2026?\n   269\tA: The Department of Commerce has not concluded the investigation by December 31, 2026.\n   270\tReason: The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or Commerce completion deadline is supplied, and the stated status is a formal investigation, not a scheduled conclusion. The evidence makes non-conclusion by December 31, 2026 more likely: Commerce is still examining access through computing capacity hosted outside China, while the reported access claims and ongoing screening activity point to a live, complex issue. These are forecasts, not proof that the investigation will remain open on the due date.\n   271\t- round-0/claude: supported | Export-control enforcement on Chinese access through Southeast Asian cloud capacity could materially change NVIDIA's Asian revenue. It is distinct from the Senate bill question. The investigation is open, complex, with no deadline, so 'not concluded' is justified.\n   272\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | The investigation concerns access to NVIDIA’s advanced chips and could affect a significant market. But an ongoing investigation and related screening provide no basis for judging whether Commerce will conclude it within the remaining months.\n   273\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported: the material shows a formal, widening investigation (offshore rented compute, Thailand GB300 claims) with no deadline or closing signal; export-control probes rarely conclude publicly within five months, so 'not concluded' is the justified default.\n   274\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | The investigation could materially affect NVIDIA’s access to customers. Its ongoing status and related screening do not establish how long Commerce investigations take or make conclusion by year-end less likely than non-conclusion.\n   275\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. The material shows a live, broadening BIS probe (offshore rented compute, Thailand GB300 claims) with no deadline or closing signal. With five months left, non-conclusion is the justified default, and the reason correctly calls it a forecast.\n   276\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The investigation could materially affect NVIDIA’s customer access. Its ongoing status and related screening do not establish a likely completion date; the asserted typical duration of export-control probes is not supplied in the material.\n   277\t\n   278\t### 28. old-1 Q28 (C115) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   279\tQ: How much will NVIDIA’s committed equity-investment obligations to ecosystem partners total at the FY2027 annual report?\n   280\tA: The disclosed amount is at least $60 billion and below $80 billion.\n   281\tReason: The company-based reference is about $43 billion—$25 billion of commitments as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027—and sits in rung 2. The broader $70 billion Bank of America estimate and evidence of substantial 2026 commitment activity support a higher balance than that reference. I estimate about $75 billion outstanding at the FY2027 report: the $70 billion estimate is the anchor, with a modest net addition for later disclosed deals, discounted for possible overlap and for investments that may be funded before the report. That remains below the $80 billion boundary for rung 4.\n   282\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | Distinct, large disclosed metric ($25B at July 26). The $75B answer anchors on BofA's cumulative $70B, which includes funded deals. Commitments get funded ($18B this year), so even with new deals the material points to rungs 1–2.\n   283\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | Equity commitments are financially material and distinct from the earlier credit-support obligations. The $70 billion estimate is not an outstanding year-end balance, while the $18 billion may overlap the $25 billion; neither justifies choosing $60–80 billion.\n   284\t\n   285\t### 29. old-1 Q44 (C026) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=figure\n   286\tQ: How much Vera CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\n   287\tA: FY2028 Vera CPU revenue is at least $30 billion and less than $40 billion.\n   288\tReason: The reference is NVIDIA management’s stated potential of $20 billion in Vera CPU revenue in FY2027 and potential for more than double that in FY2028, which implies $40 billion-plus and sits in rung 1. The implied forecast remains about $35 billion: I discount that FY2028 potential because no shipment volume or realized Vera CPU revenue is disclosed, although full production and standalone sales support execution. AMD’s reported benchmark advantages are a competitive risk but do not quantify a revenue reduction large enough to move the estimate below $30 billion. Thus the forecast stays in rung 2, below the reference’s rung.\n   289\t- round-0/claude: supported | Management frames Vera as a $20B FY2027 potential that could more than double in FY2028, a revenue-changing bet distinct from the FY2027 total-CPU question. Discounting soft 'potential' guidance, with no realized revenue and AMD competition, to about $35B is reasonable.\n   290\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Vera revenue at this scale matters and is distinct from total revenue and FY2027 CPU revenue. Management’s potential exceeds $40 billion, but the material does not substantiate a $35 billion estimate or distinguish it from neighboring ranges.\n   291\t- round-1/claude: supported | Not too thin: management explicitly framed $20B FY2027 'potential', more than doubling. That puts $40B on the rung 1/2 boundary, so a modest haircut for unrealized, hedged 'potential' guidance reasonably lands in rung 2.\n   292\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Vera revenue at this scale matters and is distinct from the earlier questions. Management’s potential exceeds $40 billion, but the material does not quantify a discount or otherwise justify $30–40 billion over neighboring ranges.\n   293\t- round-2/claude: supported | Management's reiterated $20B FY2027 'potential' more than doubling gives an explicit anchor at the $40B boundary. Haircutting hedged, unrealized upside guidance to the adjacent rung is a reasoned, material-based choice, not one made on material too thin.\n   294\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Vera revenue at this scale is material and distinct from earlier bets. Management’s more-than-$40 billion potential is a useful anchor, but the evidence does not justify a discount to $30–40 billion over neighboring ranges.\n   295\t\n   296\t### 30. old-1 Q45 (C133) answer-mark=unsupported type=yes/no\n   297\tQ: Will NVIDIA complete an investment in Anthropic’s potential IPO by September 14, 2027?\n   298\tA: NVIDIA completes an investment in Anthropic by September 14, 2027.\n   299\tReason: The reference is rung 2 (No): absent a market consensus or stated completion schedule, the default is that NVIDIA has not completed an investment by September 14, 2027. The specific Reuters-attributed reports that NVIDIA is discussing or weighing an anchor investment of up to $10 billion, together with the report that Anthropic selected Nasdaq for a potential IPO, make completion by the deadline the more likely outcome. The reported investment is not agreed and the IPO remains potential, but the roughly one-year window and concrete size of the reported discussions keep the forecast on rung 1. The additional IPO fundraising and valuation figures do not materially change that assessment.\n   300\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | A possible $10B NVIDIA stake in Anthropic is material capital and credit exposure. The answer still overrides its own 'No' reference on unagreed talks alone. Completion also needs an IPO that remains only potential within a year.\n   301\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | A potential $10 billion investment is material to NVIDIA and distinct from earlier questions. Reported discussions and a possible Nasdaq listing do not establish that an IPO and investment are more likely than not to be completed within a year.\n   302\t\n   303\t### 31. old-1 Q7 (C122) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   304\tQ: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n   305\tA: Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion and less than $1.2 trillion.\n   306\tReason: The market reference is BofA's $1.08 trillion 2027 estimate for five companies; using the carried Oracle adjustment of roughly $100–$150 billion, the four-company reference is about $930–$980 billion, in rung 3. NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion forecast for the top five, adjusted by the same Oracle amount, implies about $1.15–$1.20 trillion for these four, centered near $1.16 trillion and in rung 4. UBS's 25% 2027 growth view and financing and spending-flexibility risks pull down, while Morgan Stanley's forecast of over $1 trillion in AI infrastructure spending by the four, continued cloud growth, and NVIDIA's forecast keep the most likely outcome above $1.1 trillion. The evidence does not make $1.2 trillion or more the most likely outcome, so it does not reach rung 5.\n   307\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | 2027 hyperscaler capex drives NVIDIA revenue; a distinct year from the 2026 card. Consensus (BofA, about $930–980B for four), UBS 25% growth and Morgan Stanley's >$1T all point to rung 3; rung 4 rests on NVIDIA's interested forecast.\n   308\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | Hyperscaler spending is material to NVIDIA, and 2027 can differ from 2026. The adjusted consensus favors $930–$980 billion; Morgan Stanley’s over-$1 trillion forecast does not establish $1.1 trillion, and the reasons do not justify preferring NVIDIA’s higher estimate.\n   309\t\n   310\t### 32. old-2 Q16 (C127) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   311\tQ: How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?\n   312\tA: Total CPU revenue is greater than $25 billion.\n   313\tReason: The reference is NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU outlook, which sits at rung 3. The most likely total is just above $25 billion: the specific FY2027 Vera outlook is about $20 billion, and Grace had already exceeded $5 billion on a trailing-12-month basis during FY2027; carrying that recent Grace run-rate through the fiscal year puts the total slightly above the rung-1 boundary. Vera shipments and full production support the outlook, though the estimate is close to the boundary: Wolfe’s 2026 shipment estimate implies about $6.5 billion for calendar 2026, and AMD’s performance claims are competitive risks without a quantified revision to NVIDIA’s FY2027 outlook. The approximately $20 billion server-CPU demand figure is a headwind, but it is not an explicit cap on NVIDIA’s specific Vera sales outlook.\n   314\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | Total CPU revenue, including Grace, is a different bet from standalone Vera revenue. But 'nearly $20B' plus Grace near $5B (declining as Vera ramps) lands at or below $25B. 'Total' wording and Wolfe's figure point to rung 2–3.\n   315\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | Total CPU revenue can differ materially from standalone sales. NVIDIA’s own nearly $20 billion total-CPU outlook does not justify adding Grace’s trailing revenue to a $20 billion Vera estimate; the sources may overlap, and trailing revenue is not FY2027 revenue.\n   316\t\n   317\t### 33. old-2 Q19 (C089) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   318\tQ: Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by 2026-12-31?\n   319\tA: The Senate has not passed the Remote Access Security Act by 2026-12-31.\n   320\tReason: No explicit market consensus or Senate timetable is supplied. The observable reference is that RASA had not passed the Senate as of August 19, which sits at rung 2. The alleged remote-access cases could add pressure for legislation, but the recent evidence reports no Senate action or scheduled vote. On balance, non-passage by December 31 remains more likely.\n   321\t- round-0/claude: supported | RASA would extend export controls to cloud access, putting NVIDIA's Southeast Asian compute sales to Chinese users at risk, a material revenue issue with no earlier duplicate. Material shows no Senate action or schedule since January, so non-passage is justified.\n   322\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Remote-access export controls could materially affect demand for NVIDIA’s advanced chips. The bill’s pending status and alleged access cases do not establish whether passage or non-passage by year-end is more likely.\n   323\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported: the material shows the bill stalled in the Senate from January through August 19, with no scheduled vote. That stall points to non-passage, and the reason correctly treats the alleged access cases as pressure, not legislative progress.\n   324\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Remote-access controls could materially affect demand for NVIDIA chips. The bill’s pending status and alleged access cases provide no Senate timetable or other basis for choosing non-passage over passage by year-end.\n   325\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported: a House-passed bill stalled in the Senate from January to 19 August, with no vote scheduled, favours non-passage on base rates. The access allegations add pressure but are not legislative progress.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md | sed -n '326,396p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md | sed -n '326,396p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"   326\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Remote-access controls could materially affect NVIDIA’s chip demand. The bill remained pending through August, but the material supplies no Senate timetable or other basis for choosing non-passage over passage by year-end; it does not establish that no vote was scheduled.\n   327\t\n   328\t### 34. old-2 Q25 (C019) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   329\tQ: Will Taiwan's Ministry of Economic Affairs introduce performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by 2027-01-31?\n   330\tA: No competent Taiwanese authority formally adopts or brings into force performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by 2027-01-31.\n   331\tReason: The required outcome is formal adoption or entry into force by 2027-01-31, not consultation or consideration. Consultations are confirmed, but the Ministry gave no timeline and the controls were only reported as being weighed. That makes adoption by the deadline less likely than no adoption; the evidence does not establish that controls will never be adopted.\n   332\t- round-0/claude: supported | Taiwanese export controls on TSMC-made advanced chips could restrict NVIDIA shipments, so this is material. No earlier duplicate. The Ministry confirmed consultations but set no timeline, and controls were only being weighed, which favours no formal adoption within six months.\n   333\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Taiwanese export controls could materially affect NVIDIA’s chip supply and sales, and no earlier question settles the same outcome. Consultations without a timeline do not establish whether adoption by the deadline is more or less likely than no adoption.\n   334\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported. In a binary question the status quo is the default. Controls were only being 'weighed', and consultations had no timeline, so formal adoption within six months is less likely than not. The reason claims no more than this.\n   335\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Taiwanese export controls could materially affect NVIDIA, and no earlier question settles the same outcome. Confirmed consultations and the absence of a timeline do not establish whether formal adoption within six months is more or less likely.\n   336\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. The material shows controls only being weighed, with consultations and no timeline. That supports the status-quo answer of no formal adoption within six months. The reason claims only this lean, not certainty.\n   337\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Taiwanese controls could materially affect NVIDIA, and no earlier question settles the same outcome. Consultations without a timeline establish neither the probability nor the pace of adoption; the status quo alone does not justify choosing no adoption over adoption.\n   338\t\n   339\t### 35. old-2 Q27 (C031) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   340\tQ: Will the U.S. Department of Commerce conclude its investigation into Chinese firms' access to advanced U.S. chips by 2027-01-31?\n   341\tA: The Department of Commerce has not publicly concluded the investigation by 2027-01-31.\n   342\tReason: The reference is rung 2: the investigation is formally underway and described as likely to remain an ongoing point of contention, with no Commerce deadline or consensus supplied. The access allegations and Taiwanese smuggling enforcement show the issue remains active, but they do not report a Commerce conclusion or give a timetable; they therefore do not make a public conclusion by 2027-01-31 more likely than the investigation remaining open.\n   343\t- round-0/claude: supported | Commerce's chip-diversion probe could bring penalties or tighter controls on NVIDIA's Asian sales, so it is a real bet distinct from the Taiwan questions. The material shows an open probe with no timetable, so 'not concluded' stands.\n   344\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | The investigation concerns access to NVIDIA’s advanced chips and potentially material regulatory risk. But an ongoing point of contention does not establish how long the investigation will last; the material provides no basis to favor either deadline outcome.\n   345\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported. The probe is open, has no deadline, and is called 'likely an ongoing point of contention'. New allegations widen it. Such probes rarely conclude publicly within six months, so the status quo favours 'not concluded'.\n   346\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | The investigation concerns potentially material restrictions on advanced-chip sales. But an open investigation and ongoing contention provide no basis to favor either conclusion outcome by the deadline.\n   347\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. The material shows an open probe with no deadline, which the source says is 'likely an ongoing point of contention'. Fresh allegations and smuggling cases widen it. That favours 'not concluded' over a public conclusion within six months.\n   348\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The investigation could affect material advanced-chip sales. Its open status and ongoing contention do not establish whether a public conclusion is more or less likely by the deadline; no timetable or relevant base rate is supplied.\n   349\t\n   350\t### 36. old-2 Q29 (C153) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'unsupported']} type=figure\n   351\tQ: How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n   352\tA: Commitments are at least $50 billion and below $75 billion.\n   353\tReason: The reference is Bank of America's roughly $70 billion estimate of NVIDIA's equity investments in ecosystem partners; that sits in rung 3 ($50 billion to below $75 billion), though its period and relation to outstanding commitments are unclear. The disclosed $25 billion commitment balance plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027 gives a $43 billion base. Adding the $3.5 billion MediaTek investment announced after that remainder-of-year figure, and risk-adjusting the $10 billion Anthropic and $2.5 billion Thinking Machines discussions, implies about $53 billion. The newly reported more than $42 billion of equity stakes purchased in the first half of FY2027 confirms an exceptional pace, but it is spending rather than an additional outstanding commitment balance, so I do not add it again. The $30 billion OpenAI investment was announced before the July 26 commitment snapshot and is not counted again. The implied figure remains in rung 3, below the $75 billion boundary for rung 4.\n   354\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | Commitments of $25B against $99B of holdings can move cash, so it is worth tracking. But adding the $18B to the $25B likely double-counts. Funding will draw the year-end balance down, so rung 1–2 is likelier.\n   355\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Equity commitments are material to NVIDIA’s capital exposure and distinct from credit support. The $18 billion may overlap the $25 billion balance; the $70 billion estimate measures an unclear period and scope. Neither supports choosing the $50–75 billion range.\n   356\t- round-1/claude: unsupported | The $18B is likely part of the $25B balance, not extra. Funding draws the balance down by year-end. The $70B is a cumulative investment estimate, not outstanding commitments. Even without the double-count, the answer's own sum lands in rung 2.\n   357\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Equity commitments are material and distinct from credit support. The $18 billion may overlap the $25 billion balance, while the $70 billion estimate has unclear scope. Future commitments and funding are too uncertain to choose a year-end range.\n   358\t- round-2/claude: unsupported | The $18B is likely the in-year part of the $25B balance, so adding it double-counts. Funding then draws the balance down. Without that, the answer's own sum is about $35B, in rung 2. The $70B measures investments, not commitments.\n   359\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Equity commitments are material and distinct from credit support. The $18 billion may overlap the $25 billion balance, and the $70 billion estimate has unclear scope. Future commitments and payments are too uncertain to favor a range.\n   360\t\n   361\t### 37. old-2 Q39 (C172) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   362\tQ: Will the U.S. Justice Department conclude its antitrust review of NVIDIA’s Groq transaction by 2027-01-31?\n   363\tA: The Justice Department has not publicly concluded the review by 2027-01-31.\n   364\tReason: The reference is rung 2: no market consensus or DOJ completion timetable is supplied, and the review is reported to be active. The investigation and reported information request make a public conclusion by the deadline less likely than the review remaining open. The transaction’s scale and the legal and congressional scrutiny add context for a substantive review, but do not establish a conclusion date. The reported view that DOJ is unlikely to require an unwind concerns the possible remedy, not whether or when the review will conclude.\n   365\t- round-0/claude: supported | A DOJ antitrust review of a $17–20B Groq deal can bring material legal or remedy risk, and no earlier question covers it. The active probe, recent information request and lack of any timetable favour no public conclusion by January 2027.\n   366\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | The review concerns a multibillion-dollar transaction, making it worth tracking. An active inquiry and information request establish no completion timetable or basis for choosing whether public conclusion is more likely before or after the deadline.\n   367\t- round-1/claude: supported | The material shows an active probe with a recent formal information request and no settlement or timetable. Such investigations rarely end publicly within four months, so 'not concluded' is favoured over its neighbour, not left undetermined.\n   368\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | The multibillion-dollar transaction makes the review worth tracking. The active inquiry and undated information request provide no basis for judging whether public conclusion is more likely before or after January 31.\n   369\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. The probe is active nine months in, with a formal information request outstanding and no timetable or settlement signs. DOJ rarely announces conclusions publicly, so the material favours 'not concluded' and is not too thin.\n   370\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The transaction’s scale makes the review worth tracking. The inquiry is active, but the information request is undated and no completion timetable or relevant base rate is supplied to favor either deadline outcome.\n   371\t\n   372\t### 38. old-2 Q6 (C166) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   373\tQ: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n   374\tA: Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion and less than $1.2 trillion.\n   375\tReason: The market reference is approximately $1.08 trillion for calendar 2027, which is rung 3. The implied estimate remains about $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate four-to-five share proxy (about $730 billion of $800 billion) to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five estimate. That is above rung 4’s $1.1 trillion floor but below rung 5’s $1.2 trillion floor. New grid-connection and other execution constraints increase downside risk, but the evidence does not quantify a reduction sufficient to cross either boundary; repeated reports of the $1.3 trillion estimate do not independently raise it. The share proxy is approximate because the underlying figures do not have perfectly matched scope.\n   376\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | Big-4 2027 capex drives NVIDIA revenue. Independent BofA consensus is $1.08T for five companies including Oracle, so about $1T for four (rung 3). The reason ignores this and adopts NVIDIA's self-interested $1.3T proxy despite grid-freeze downside.\n   377\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Hyperscaler spending is material to NVIDIA, and 2026 and 2027 outcomes can differ. The $1.19 trillion estimate relies on a mismatched 2026 spending proxy and an unverified stable share; the competing $1.08 trillion estimate covers five companies.\n   378\t- round-1/claude: unsupported | Material points to rung 3. BofA's $1.08T covers five companies including Oracle, and UBS's 25% growth on $730B gives about $910B. The reason admits the market reference is rung 3 but adopts NVIDIA's mismatched-scope $1.19T proxy, ignoring downside risks.\n   379\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Hyperscaler spending is material to NVIDIA, and 2026 and 2027 are distinct outcomes. The $1.19 trillion estimate depends on a mismatched, unverified share proxy; BofA’s lower estimate covers five companies. Neither establishes which rung is better supported.\n   380\t- round-2/claude: unsupported | Not thin: BofA $1.08T (five incl. Oracle), UBS 25% on ~$730B (~$910B), and Benzinga's $916B-to-$1.2T interpolation all point to rung 3. The reason concedes rung 3, then follows one NVIDIA-sourced, scope-mismatched proxy.\n   381\t- round-2/codex: unsupported | Hyperscaler spending is material to NVIDIA, and 2027 is a distinct outcome from 2026. BofA’s $1.08 trillion estimate covers five companies, pointing below $1.1 trillion for four; the selected rung relies on an unsupported, mismatched-scope share proxy.\n   382\t\n   383\t### 39. old-2 Q9 (C150) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   384\tQ: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n   385\tA: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion.\n   386\tReason: The market reference is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which is rung 2. The evidence-based estimate is now around $410 billion: NVIDIA reported $164 billion in the first half, Q3 total-revenue guidance and the recent Data Center mix imply roughly $100 billion for Q3, and a roughly $146 billion Q4 is supported by the expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp. SemiAnalysis's forecast of second-half Data Center revenue 20% above analyst estimates is a meaningful upside input: applying it to the roughly $250 billion of second-half revenue implied by the $414 billion reference would point to about $464 billion for the year. I discount that forecast because it does not state its underlying estimate and its implied Q4 is much higher than the company has quantified; the resulting central estimate remains near $410 billion. That crosses the $400 billion boundary into rung 2, but not the $450 billion boundary. Supply and competition risks, and NVIDIA's exclusion of China compute revenue from its outlook, temper the upside.\n   387\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | FY27 Data Center revenue is a core bet; no earlier listed question duplicates it. Q4 jumps from ~$122B to $146B (+46% sequentially, versus a ~12% Q3 guide) without new quantified evidence, despite supply-constraint items; rung 3 fits better.\n   388\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | Data Center revenue is central to NVIDIA’s business and distinct from the earlier questions. The $146 billion Q4 estimate requires roughly 46% sequential growth; qualitative hyperscale reacceleration and the Rubin ramp do not justify that jump over the previous estimate.\n   389\t\n   390\t### 40. old-3 Q14 (C021) answer-mark=unsupported type=figure\n   391\tQ: What will NVIDIA report as total CPU revenue for FY2027?\n   392\tA: Total CPU revenue is at least $25 billion.\n   393\tReason: The reference is NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU outlook, which sits at rung 2; it is not a forecast of total CPU revenue. Adding Grace’s reported trailing-12-month revenue of more than $5 billion as the available run-rate puts total CPU revenue just above $25 billion, crossing rung 1’s boundary. Vera is in full production, shipments are underway, and customer deployments support the $20 billion outlook. AMD’s performance claims and reports of customers designing their own CPUs are downside risks, but they do not quantify a reduction to NVIDIA’s FY2027 outlook or establish a Grace decline.\n   394\t- round-0/claude: unsupported | A ~$20B+ CPU line can move NVIDIA revenue and profit. NVIDIA itself calls ~$20B its 'total CPU'/'total server CPU' figure. Adding a backward-looking, fading Grace run-rate to 'nearly $20B' only edges past $25B, and risks double-counting.\n   395\t- round-0/codex: unsupported | CPU revenue at this scale is material and distinct from total company revenue. Nearly $20 billion plus Grace’s trailing revenue does not establish FY2027 revenue above $25 billion: Grace may decline, and the figures’ scopes may overlap.\n   396\t\n     1\t# Phase 1, step 1: census of the judge's rejected answers ($0, read by Claude, 2026-11-20)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Scope.** 49 answers in the 5 stored draws of the release comparison that the readers rejected or split, among questions rated worth\n     4\ttracking (`rejected-answers.md`). The frozen judging-v7 gave all of them. Planted reader controls are excluded: they were filtered by the\n     5\tdeck key's role, `product` only.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Two populations\n     8\t| Group | Count | What it is |\n     9\t|---|---|---|\n    10\t| **Reader-threshold splits** (Claude supported, Codex insufficient) | 23 | Mostly deadline yes/no questions answered with the status quo (\"still open\", \"not passed\"). Codex asks for a base rate that the material does not hold; Claude accepts the status quo. This is the families' known threshold gap, not a judge fault agreed by both. **Not the target** |\n    11\t| **Genuine splits** (supported against unsupported) | 2 | #13 France, #16 the Groq-licensed China chip |\n    12\t| **Rejected by both readers** (unsupported or insufficient on both sides) | 24 | **The target** |\n    13\t\n    14\t## The 24, by mechanism (one primary class each)\n    15\t| Class | Count | Cases (number in `rejected-answers.md`) | Example |\n    16\t|---|---|---|---|\n    17\t| **O: adds amounts that overlap, or counts a factor twice** | 6 | 32, 40 (Grace's trailing revenue added to a \"total CPU\" outlook); 36, 45 ($18B added to a $25B balance that likely holds it); 44 (an above-consensus uplift stacked on an above-consensus run-rate); 47 (memory costs already inside guidance) | old-3 Q3: $446B revenue by stacking uplifts, where consensus and run-rate sit in rung 2 |\n    18\t| **S: a figure that measures something else** | 6 | 31, 38, 49 (five companies' total capex and NVIDIA's own forecast for four companies' data-center capex); 28 (a cumulative investment estimate for an outstanding balance); 5 (a lease NVIDIA holds as lessee counted as a guarantee); 8 (a partner outside the question's four) | old-2 Q6: NVIDIA's $1.3T top-five forecast scaled by a 2026 share, against $1.08T consensus for five |\n    19\t| **E: an estimate or adjustment with no basis** | 5 | 39 (+46% sequential Q4); 48 (an arbitrary trim to just below $40B); 4 (28% with no denominator); 17 (a sum $0.1B under a boundary, from approximate parts); 1 (one state, with none qualifying) | old-3 Q41: guidance points above $40B; trimmed to $38–39B on unquantified risk |\n    20\t| **W: reports of talks taken as a likely completion** | 2 | 30, 42 | old-3 Q23: early-stage financing talks turn the status-quo \"No\" into \"Yes\" |\n    21\t| **R: a rung's definition misapplied** | 2 | 12, 20 (rung 2 needs a formal decision after the opening date; the reported delay predates it) | new-2 Q5 Kyber |\n    22\t| **M: too little material, default chosen** | 3 | 6, 15 (both readers: too thin); 11 (status quo against rich material) | — |\n    23\t\n    24\t## What cuts across the classes\n    25\t- **The answer leaves the reference's rung on a weak step of its own, in about 16 of 24.** The reference is the consensus, guidance or\n    26\t  status quo that the judge itself names first. Cases: 5, 8, 12, 17, 20, 28, 30, 31, 32, 38, 40, 42, 44, 47, 48 and 49. The readers'\n    27\t  rejections say, in effect, that the reference rung was right and the step off it is not justified.\n    28\t- **The step lands just across a boundary in 7:** 5, 17, 32, 40, 44, 48 and 49. Examples are $24.9B against $25B, \"just above $25B\",\n    29\t  \"just above $1.1T\" and $38–39B against $40B.\n    30\t- **The step off is asymmetric.** The same answers refuse to move on unquantified downside (\"does not quantify a reduction sufficient to\n    31\t  cross\"), yet move on unquantified upside (31, 38, 44, 49), and the reverse in 47 and 48.\n    32\t- **On the 32 matters:** M08 (36, 45, 28) is O or S, and M14 (31, 38, 49) is S. Both are in the target's two largest classes.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Not yet established (next step: mechanism)\n    35\t- Which sentence of judging-v7 lets the answer leave the reference on its own arithmetic, and whether the request defines overlap,\n    36\t  scope or the boundary.\n    37\t- Whether the judge's own account names the same sentence.\n    38\t- Whether a re-send gives the same answer. The judge is a sampler: the 24 are one draw each, though M08 and M14 recur across draws.\n    39\t\n    40\t## Errors found while doing this\n    41\t- My report to Alex on 2026-11-19 cited an old-2 answer that \"chose $75–100B against its own estimate of about $53B\". That card, C140,\n    42\t  is a planted reader control. The real old-2 answer, C153, chose $50–75B and was rejected for overlap. Corrected in the merge test's\n    43\t  `RESULT.md` and in `PLAN.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md | sed -n '220,244p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '1,180p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/reader-brief.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md; rg -n '\"'^## D26[034]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md | sed -n '220,244p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '1,180p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/reader-brief.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md; rg -n '\"'^## D26[034]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"   220\t- round-2/claude: supported | The question resolves on NVIDIA's separately disclosed amount, not project cost. The material shows NVIDIA reporting only an aggregate $119B and unpriced Zayo, optics and Corning deals, so rung 1 is the reasoned forecast.\n   221\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The project could be material and is distinct from total supply commitments. The evidence does not size NVIDIA’s attributable commitments or indicate what it will disclose by year-end, so it does not favor below $2.5 billion over the other ranges.\n   222\t\n   223\t### 23. old-1 Q16 (C098) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   224\tQ: Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by December 31, 2026?\n   225\tA: The Senate has not passed RASA by December 31, 2026.\n   226\tReason: No market consensus is supplied. The deadline reference is passage by December 31, 2026 (rung 1); the alternative is that the Senate has not passed RASA by then (rung 2). RASA had passed the House but was still awaiting Senate action on July 23, and the August 19 report says it had still not passed. With about four months remaining and no stated Senate timetable or movement, the evidence favors no passage by the deadline. Reports of remote chip access and the gap in existing controls increase the policy case for action, but do not indicate that the Senate is moving toward a vote, so they do not overcome the stalled status.\n   227\t- round-0/claude: supported | RASA would extend export controls to cloud access to NVIDIA chips, a regulatory bet that could change China-linked revenue; no earlier card covers it. Bill stalled in Senate as of August 19 with no timetable, supporting no passage.\n   228\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Remote-access export controls could materially affect demand for NVIDIA’s advanced chips. But a bill awaiting Senate action, without evidence about its prospects or timetable, is too thin a basis to favor either deadline outcome.\n   229\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported: a House-passed bill still stalled in the Senate seven months later, with no timetable or scheduled vote and four months left, justifies the status-quo answer. Most such bills never pass, so the material is not too thin.\n   230\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Remote-access export controls could materially affect demand for NVIDIA chips. The bill’s pending status and absence of a reported timetable do not establish whether passage or nonpassage by year-end is more likely.\n   231\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported: the material shows the bill stalled in the Senate from January to August 19, with no scheduled vote. With four months left, that justifies the default no-passage answer, and the reasons follow the material.\n   232\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | Remote-access controls could materially affect NVIDIA’s chip demand. The bill’s pending status and lack of a reported Senate timetable do not establish whether passage or nonpassage by year-end is more likely.\n   233\t\n   234\t### 24. old-1 Q20 (C175) answer-mark={'split': ['insufficient', 'supported']} type=yes/no\n   235\tQ: Will NVIDIA agree to finance OpenAI chip purchases for the southern Ohio data center project by January 31, 2027?\n   236\tA: NVIDIA has not agreed to finance OpenAI chip purchases for the project by 2027-01-31.\n   237\tReason: The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus, NVIDIA guidance, or stated plan says NVIDIA will agree to finance OpenAI’s chip purchases by January 31, 2027. The specific reports and NVIDIA’s statement establish discussions of up to $350 billion in GPU financing, but discussions are not an agreement. NVIDIA’s disclosed commitments are instead guarantees for land, power, and shell buildout, and the reported vendor-financing denial weighs against those discussions becoming a chip-purchase financing commitment by the deadline. The evidence therefore leaves No more likely than Yes and does not cross the rung boundary.\n   238\t- round-0/claude: supported | Financing up to $350B of OpenAI GPU purchases could change NVIDIA's revenue and credit risk; the earlier guarantee question is a separate bet. Only preliminary talks are reported, while signed commitments cover land, power and shell, so No holds.\n   239\t- round-0/codex: insufficient | Potential chip financing of up to $350 billion is material and distinct from the earlier facility guarantee. Talks establish a possibility, but the evidence gives too little basis to judge whether agreement by the deadline is more likely than not.\n   240\t- round-1/claude: supported | Keep supported. Talks were confirmed but stayed preliminary as of mid-August. The signed filing covers only land, power and shell, and NVIDIA denied vendor financing. That is enough to choose No over Yes, so the material is not too thin.\n   241\t- round-1/codex: insufficient | Potential chip financing is material and distinct from the facility guarantee. Preliminary talks and a general denial of vendor financing do not provide enough evidence to judge whether an agreement by the deadline is more likely than not.\n   242\t- round-2/claude: supported | Keep supported. Talks were confirmed but preliminary and could collapse. The August filing committed only land/power/shell guarantees, with no chip financing, and NVIDIA denied vendor financing. With no agreement and four months left, No over Yes is justified.\n   243\t- round-2/codex: insufficient | The potential financing is material and distinct from the facility guarantee. Preliminary talks and a denial of current vendor financing do not establish whether an agreement by January is more or less likely than not.\n   244\t\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\n     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n     9\t- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n    10\t- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n    11\t- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n     1\t\"\"\"06-views.md step 7: one re-judging round. Open views whose reading changed are judged in dependency order, each\n     2\tonce; a view whose conclusion changed adds its open dependants. The model reads the evidence in force (with each\n     3\treplaced predecessor), the dependencies' current conclusions and its own last conclusion (for comparison only).\n     4\tCode checks every citation and that a rung move or a first judgement says changed; one retry, then the item fails.\n     5\t\n     6\tThe request is judging-v7 (D354, frozen with steps 3 and 4): no other version is built, and a configuration that names another is\n     7\trefused before any call. Every answer is stored in the canonical vocabulary.\n     8\t\n     9\tThe theme block (D191, D195): an asset thesis is judged with every open, judged theme thesis in view and answers, in theme_pushes,\n    10\twhich way each theme it weighed pushes it; theme theses are judged before asset theses in a round, and a theme judgement that says\n    11\tchanged queues every open asset thesis with evidence in force, once. The round's queue is derived from the ledger (the day's changed\n    12\tviews, the dependants of views judged at this sequence number with a changed conclusion, and the asset theses a changed theme queues),\n    13\tso a resumed round recovers what an earlier commit had queued.\n    14\t\n    15\tThe evidence in view (D198): a judgement reads the arrivals and the basis among the evidence in force, not everything in force.\n    16\t\n    17\tThe reference (D260): the rung is the forecast the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects\n    18\t(consensus, guidance, the stated plan); the answer states the reference and the outcome the evidence implies, both stored beside the\n    19\trung, and an empty one is refused.\"\"\"\n    20\timport dataclasses\n    21\timport json\n    22\timport re\n    23\t\n    24\tfrom .. import config, model, vocabulary\n    25\tfrom . import store\n    26\t\n    27\tPUSHES = vocabulary.PUSHES\n    28\tSUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('judging-v7',)   # D354: the frozen judging prompt\n    29\tREADINGS = 5                      # a piece is shown in the thesis's first five judgements after it arrives\n    30\tBASIS = 10                        # and while one of the last ten judgements cited it\n    31\tTHEME_REASONS_CHARS = 300\n    32\tUPDATED_MARK = 'updated since this thesis was last judged'\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef require_supported(prompt_version):\n    36\t    \"\"\"Refuses a judging prompt version this code does not build, before any request is made.\"\"\"\n    37\t    if prompt_version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    38\t        raise ValueError(f'judging {prompt_version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\", \".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D354)')\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\n    42\t    \"\"\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\n    43\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\n    44\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    45\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    46\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    47\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    48\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    49\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    50\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    51\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef schema_for(prompt_version):\n    55\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    56\t    pushes = PUSHES\n    57\t    schema = {\n    58\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n    59\t        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n    60\t        'properties': {\n    61\t            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\n    62\t            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n    63\t            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n    64\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n    65\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n    66\t        },\n    67\t    }\n    68\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n    69\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n    70\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n    71\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n    72\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n    73\t    return schema\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n    77\t    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n    78\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n    79\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n    80\t        return []\n    81\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n    82\t    out = []\n    83\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\"):\n    84\t        theme_id = row['view_id']\n    85\t        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n    86\t        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\n    87\t            continue\n    88\t        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\n    89\t                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\n    90\t        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\n    91\t        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\n    92\t    return out\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\tSTANCE_FIELDS = ['reference', 'implied_outcome']   # D260: what the market expects, and the figure or date the evidence implies\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\tclass JudgementRefused(Exception):\n    99\t    pass\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef topological(conn, view_ids):\n   103\t    \"\"\"Dependencies first: a view comes after every view it depends on that is also in the set.\"\"\"\n   104\t    remaining = list(dict.fromkeys(view_ids))\n   105\t    ordered, placed = [], set()\n   106\t    while remaining:\n   107\t        progressed = False\n   108\t        for view_id in list(remaining):\n   109\t            deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   110\t            if deps.isdisjoint(set(remaining) - {view_id}) or deps <= placed:\n   111\t                ordered.append(view_id)\n   112\t                placed.add(view_id)\n   113\t                remaining.remove(view_id)\n   114\t                progressed = True\n   115\t        if not progressed:                 # a cycle slipped through: keep going in the given order\n   116\t            ordered.extend(remaining)\n   117\t            break\n   118\t    return ordered\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0):\n   122\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown.\"\"\"\n   123\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   124\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   125\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   126\t    if hidden:\n   127\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   128\t    for p in pieces:\n   129\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   130\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   131\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   132\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   133\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   134\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   135\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   136\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   137\t    if deps:\n   138\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   139\t        for d in deps:\n   140\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   141\t            if not target:\n   142\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   143\t                continue\n   144\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   145\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   146\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   147\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   148\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   149\t    if themes:\n   150\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   151\t        for theme in themes:\n   152\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   153\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   154\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   155\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   156\t    if last:\n   157\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   158\t    else:\n   159\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   160\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   161\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   162\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   163\t    return lines\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   167\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   168\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   169\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   170\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   171\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   172\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   173\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes_in_force(conn, view_id), hidden=hidden)\n   174\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   175\t        return handle.read(), '\\n'.join(lines)\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   179\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   180\t\n     1\t# Brief for the analyst reader\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst who follows NVIDIA. It is the evening of 2026-07-14. You have in front of you everything an analyst\n     4\tfollowing the company would have noted from the news of 2026-07-01 to 2026-07-14: the items in `packet-v1.json` (each with an id `iNNN`,\n     5\tthe publication day, the article title, the source tier, who said it, the exact passage and its meaning). You are asked, for each open\n     6\tquestion in `questions-v1.json`, where you stand tonight and why.\n     7\t\n     8\tUse only the material in the packet. Do not use anything you know from outside it, and do not guess what happened after 2026-07-14.\n     9\tEvery claim you make must cite item ids from the packet. If the packet carries nothing about a question, say so (`no_view: true`) rather\n    10\tthan reasoning from general knowledge.\n    11\t\n    12\tHow an analyst forms a stance (these are the house rules, quoted):\n    13\t- \"A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument weighed against what is priced.\"\n    14\t  So first establish what the market expected for the question as of 2026-07-14 (a consensus figure, the company's guidance, the stated\n    15\t  plan or deadline), then ask what the evidence implies, then compare the two.\n    16\t- \"Only facts can establish which rung holds.\" Published figures, official actions and completed transactions fix what is known; company\n    17\t  guidance and management statements are the strongest forward input; analyst and media views and rumours move the view in proportion to\n    18\t  their specificity (a number, a date, a named party). \"A repeat is not new evidence, and model agreement is not corroboration\": the same\n    19\t  claim in several outlets counts once.\n    20\t- \"Lean cautious, catch the increment\": most of what is written is noise; new information that changes the answer is never missed.\n    21\t- Work the numbers where they exist: reported quarters and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a\n    22\t  supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A part cannot exceed the whole it belongs to; a figure that spans\n    23\t  several periods or products gives a question only its share.\n    24\t- Say how far the material settles the matter (confidence), and name the strongest item against your view.\n    25\t\n    26\tWrite one JSON object per question, exactly in this shape (numbers as plain numbers in the question's `unit`; use null where a field does\n    27\tnot apply):\n    28\t\n    29\t{\n    30\t  \"question_id\": \"q01\",\n    31\t  \"no_view\": false,\n    32\t  \"reference\": {\"text\": \"what the market expected and where it comes from, or 'none stated: status quo is ...'\", \"value\": 392000000000, \"items\": [\"i034\"]},\n    33\t  \"implied_outcome\": {\"text\": \"the outcome the material implies and how you derived it\", \"low\": 395000000000, \"high\": 420000000000, \"yes_no\": null, \"items\": [\"i012\", \"i040\"]},\n    34\t  \"direction\": \"above | in_line | below | yes | no\",\n    35\t  \"confidence\": \"high | medium | low\",\n    36\t  \"decisive_items\": [\"i012\", \"i040\", \"i077\"],\n    37\t  \"against\": {\"text\": \"the strongest item against the view, or null\", \"items\": [\"i090\"]},\n    38\t  \"reasoning\": \"three to six sentences, every claim with item ids\"\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\tFor a yes/no question set `implied_outcome.yes_no` to true or false and `low`/`high` to null; `direction` is then \"yes\" or \"no\". For a\n    42\tnumeric question give `low` and `high` as the range you would bet on (a point estimate is low = high); `direction` compares that range\n    43\twith `reference.value` (in_line when the range contains the reference or the difference is within the noise of the estimate).\n     1\t# 判断的尺子，第 1 版（D3 立场金标）\n     2\t\n     3\t写于 2026-11-02。Alex 的话：\"你已经改了好几次尺子了，到底什么是对的，以及你怎么 freeze。\"\n     4\t\n     5\t## 0. 一句话\n     6\t\n     7\t一道题判得对不对，拿它和**一位资深对冲基金分析师读完同样 14 天材料后的看法**比：他认为市场原来预期什么、材料推出来的结果是多少、\n     8\t相对预期是高是低；系统最后一次判断落的那一档，有没有把这个结果包进去。分析师不是我，不是写代码的人，不看系统的输出；他的看法写成文件、算出\n     9\tsha256、记进决定，之后一个字不改。\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. 什么是\"对\"\n    12\t\n    13\t- **单位**：一道金标题 × 一个时点（14 天窗口末，2026-07-14 收盘后）。23 道题：22 道种子（`poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json` v1–v22，每次运行里\n    14\t  编号固定）加金标 must_open 里种子没覆盖的 1 道（俄亥俄租约担保是/否，2026-07-01 的 must_open）。其余 27 条 must_open 都是这 23 道的同一赌注\n    15\t  （信用支持金额 ×10、Kyber 出货 ×11、云厂商资本开支 ×5、内存价格 ×1、中国放行 H200 ×2），映射写在 `questions-v1.json` 里，Alex 签。\n    16\t- **材料**：签过的抽取标准对这 14 天的读法，即金标 golden-v5（dev，118 篇）的 309 条事项（核心 86、辅助 151、可选 72），带日期、标题、\n    17\t  来源层、说话人、原文和意思。不用系统的账本（账本随每臂变，尺子不能随臂变），不用原始全文（那是重做抽取）。这和抽取的尺子是同一把：标准第 5 节\n    18\t  说的\"分析员会记的\"就是这些。\n    19\t- **分析师写什么**（每道题一条，`reader-brief.md` 是他拿到的全部说明，里面只有标准和 PRD 06 的原话，没有系统的提示词）：\n    20\t  1. `reference`：到 2026-07-14 为止市场预期这道题的答案是什么（一致预期、公司指引、既定计划或截止日），出自哪几条事项；材料里没有就写\n    21\t     \"没有，参照 = 现状\"。\n    22\t  2. `implied_outcome`：材料推出来的结果——数字题给一个数或一个区间，事件题给是/否和日期——怎么推的，出自哪几条。\n    23\t  3. `direction`：结果相对参照：above / in_line / below；事件题 yes / no。\n    24\t  4. `confidence`：high / medium / low（材料把这件事定到什么程度）。\n    25\t  5. `decisive_items`：撑起这个看法的 2–6 条事项编号；`against`：最强的反面一条。\n    26\t  6. `no_view`：材料里没有任何关于这道题的东西时为 true；这道题不进分数，记\"没练到\"。\n    27\t  7. `reasoning`：三到六句。只用材料，不用材料外的知识，每个说法都要有编号。\n    28\t- **分析师是谁**：两位互相独立、都没写过这套代码也没看过系统输出的模型读者（A：Codex；B：一个干净上下文的 Claude 读者），各自从同一个包\n    29\t  写一遍。都标明\"模型写的\"。**Alex 定（2026-11-02，D262）：金标 = 读者 B 的 23 条答案，原样；读者 A 的答案留作对照记录**，两者的差别\n    30\t  （区间或是/否不同 3/23：q09、q12、q23；方向标签不同 12/20）就是这把尺子自身噪声的记录（`reconcile-v1.md`）。\n    31\t- **判\"对\"的方法**（`score_judgement.py`，全部是代码）：取一次运行里每道题在 2026-07-14 及之前最后一次判断。数字题：金标的区间\n    32\t  [low, high] 和系统所选那一档的 [lo, hi) 有没有交集，有 = 一致；事件题：是/否相同 = 一致。没判过的题单独数（那是证据没到，D2 的事，不算\n    33\t  判断错）。另外打印两条零假设：**查表基线**（把金标写的参照数落进哪一档，就选那一档）和**永远中性基线**；判断要在这两条线之上才算有判断力。\n    34\t  读者之间的分歧率一起打印，那是尺子自身的噪声。\n    35\t- **第二层，读不是数**：分数之外，对一个样本的判断，由没写代码的读者看系统写的理由（从 judging-v6 起还有 reference 和 implied_outcome）\n    36\t  是不是从所示证据得出。这是 AGENTS §7.2 的\"分数是线索、trace 是测量\"。\n    37\t\n    38\t## 2. 怎么 freeze\n    39\t\n    40\t原则先于机制（D261，Alex 2026-11-02：\"我们做完的 review 过的尺子金标不能再动了\"）：这一页、读者说明、题单和金标在 Alex 审过签字之后一个字不改；之前只在建的过程中改，签字前不拿它打任何分。下面是把这句话变成代码和文件的做法。\n    41\t\n    42\t1. 读者只看 `packet-v1.json` 和 `reader-brief.md`，看不到任何运行、账本、提示词；读者的原始答案 `reader-A.json`、`reader-B.json` 原样保存，不改。\n    43\t2. 我不写金标。我做的只有：拼包（代码）、按 direction 机械对齐两位读者、把分歧按材料写成对照记录（引编号）；分歧由材料定，定不了的列给 Alex。\n    44\t3. 金标文件 `gold-v1.json` 带 `ruler_version: 1`、两位读者的 sha256、每道题的来源（A/B 一致，或裁定及理由）；文件的 sha256 写进\n    45\t   `gold-v1.sha256` 和决定 D261。Alex 签的是：23 道题的清单和映射、裁定过的题。签之前每个分数都标\"金标第 1 版，未签\"。\n    46\t4. `score_judgement.py` 开头读金标的 sha256 和 `ruler_version`，和自己写死的对不上就拒绝打分，打印两边的 sha；每份分数都印金标版本。\n    47\t5. 冻住后不改文件。发现错了，写进 `corrections-v1.json` 一条带日期的记录：哪道题、改前、改后、为什么；打分器不悄悄应用它，只在分数旁印\n    48\t   \"有 N 条更正未并入\"。更正积累到要并入时，出第 2 版：新文件、新 sha、决定里记，旧分数作废并说明。\n    49\t6. 这一页的定义本身改了（单位、材料、字段、判对的方法），就是第 2 版尺子：金标必须重写，打分器拒绝版本不符的金标。改定义只能由记录在 Alex\n    50\t   原话上的决定触发（AGENTS §7.1）。\n    51\t7. 一把尺子：判断这一步不再有别的评分标准。我昨天定的判断规则 D260 是系统这边的规则，不是尺子；读者的说明里没有它。\n    52\t\n    53\t**冻结记录**：2026-11-02，`gold-v1.json` sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2`，写在 `gold-v1.sha256` 和 `score_judgement.py` 里；`corrections-v1.json` 为空。当天下午提过的两条改法（读者分叉时打三档分；五五开的题不计分）Alex 没采纳：一题一个区间，每题都算。\n    54\t\n    55\t这把尺子作为整体（抽取标准 + 题目 + 判断）写在 AGENTS §7.1 \"The frozen ruler\"，每个文件的 sha256 由 `tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` 守着：任何一个动了，整套测试变红。\n    56\t\n    57\t## 2′. 这把尺子沿用了什么，新的只有哪一层\n    58\t\n    59\t沿用、不重做：抽取标准页（第 3 版签字 D243 + D250 的四条界线）和 golden-v5 是这把尺子的**材料**，按 sha 引用（`packet-v1.json` 记了金标的 sha）；golden-v5 的题目部分（28 条 must_open，题目标准第 3 版）映射进 23 道题；种子 v2（D253）给题的身份和档的边界；PRD 06 的判断规则和 AGENTS §8 的分析师原话是读者说明里的全部规则；桌面尺子 README 的 D1、D2 不动。2026-10-27 的步骤 3/4 金标（`research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/`，24 例，量的是重复 / 替换 / 并入的决定，不是档位）里写的分析师标准 A（谁先说的，复述只加一个出处不加事实）、B（期间和定义要对上，季度不是全年）和这份说明一致，两者量的是不同步骤；那份金标是在旧账本上写的，助手自己写的，当时就标了不是独立金标。新的只有一层：判断这一步的档位从来没有金标，这是第一份，还有打分器。\n    60\t\n    61\t## 3. 这把尺子不量什么\n    62\t\n    63\t该开的题开了没有（D1）、证据挂得对不对（D2）、14 天里每天的路径、依赖和主题推力。它只量：窗口末，系统的档位有没有包住分析师认为的结果。\n    64\t\n    65\t## 4. 已知的弱点，写明\n    66\t\n    67\t- 读者是模型，不是人。金标是一位读者（B）的看法，Alex 选的；另一位（A）留作对照，两者在 3/23 道题上区间不交，这是尺子的噪声下限；Alex 的裁定是人的那一票。\n    68\t- 材料外的知识：事后结果（FY2027 年报、2026 年底 Rubin 出不出货）都在模型知识截止之后，无法作弊；但模型可能用它记得的\"常识\"补材料，说明里\n    69\t  禁止并要求每句引编号，对照时查。\n    70\t- 参照：材料里不一定有每道题的一致预期（内存价格、CoWoS 产能），那时参照是现状，direction 的意义弱一点，分数仍按区间交集算。\n    71\t- 种子的档不是围着一致预期写的（总收入题一致预期 $392B 落在中性档 350–400 的上沿）：所以分数不比\"看涨/看跌\"的标签，只比区间有没有包住。\n    72\t\n    73\t## 5. 文件\n    74\t\n    75\t`judgement-gold/`：`ruler-v1.md`（本页）、`reader-brief.md`、`build_packet.py` → `packet-v1.json` + `questions-v1.json`、\n    76\t`run_reader_codex.py` → `reader-A.json`、读者 B 的答案 `reader-B.json`、`reconcile.py` → `gold-v1.json` + `reconcile-v1.md`、\n    77\t`gold-v1.sha256`、`corrections-v1.json`、`score_judgement.py`。\n3049:## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n3069:## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\n3075:## D264 · 2026-11-02 · The extraction reads the day's open questions with their takes lines and files the statements itself (extraction v72, poc-v92): the one-decider architecture Alex chose is built and measured against poc-v91 on the frozen ruler\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3049,3075p'; ls -l poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account; nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,78p'; rg -n 'class|replay|scope|overlap' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3049,3075p'; ls -l poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account; nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | sed -n '1,78p'; rg -n 'class|replay|scope|overlap' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"  3049\t## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n  3050\t\n  3051\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\n  3052\t- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\n  3053\t- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\n  3054\t- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n  3055\t\n  3056\t## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\n  3057\t\n  3058\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\".\n  3059\t- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \"假的测量\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\n  3060\t- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\n  3061\t- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\n  3062\t\n  3063\t## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\n  3064\t\n  3065\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, after reading the two readers' reasoning on every disagreement (readers A and B differed on 3 of 23 questions by range or yes/no and on 12 of 20 direction labels; the system disagreed with the draft on the total revenue and Vera CPU questions in every draw): \"那就不要理A了；我们就go with B 好吧，定下尺子金表\".\n  3066\t- Fixed by that decision: the ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md` (unit: a gold question at the window end 2026-07-14; material: golden-v5's 309 items by sha; a numeric question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match; the two null baselines printed with every score); the question list and the must_open mapping as built (`questions-v1.json`, 22 seeds + the Ohio guarantee); the gold `gold-v1.json` = reader B's 23 answers verbatim (B: a fresh-context Claude reader, model-authored, 3 questions marked no material: CoWoS capacity, semiconductor growth, SK Telecom), sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2` in `gold-v1.sha256` and in `score_judgement.py`, which refuses any other. Reader A (Codex) stays beside it as the control record (`reader-A.json`, `reconcile-v1.md`): its distance from B is the stick's own noise. Claude's two proposals of the afternoon (a three-level score when readers split; toss-up questions excluded) were not adopted: one range per question, every question counts. From here D261 applies: nothing in the ruler or the gold changes; a defect is a dated record in `corrections-v1.json`.\n  3067\t- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \"no judgement\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\n  3068\t\n  3069\t## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\n  3070\t\n  3071\t- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \"wrong\" on some questions: \"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\n  3072\t- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\n  3073\t- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\n  3074\t\n  3075\t## D264 · 2026-11-02 · The extraction reads the day's open questions with their takes lines and files the statements itself (extraction v72, poc-v92): the one-decider architecture Alex chose is built and measured against poc-v91 on the frozen ruler\ntotal 192\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1461 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q11.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1521 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q20.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1536 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q26.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1410 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q27.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1415 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q31.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1556 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q4.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1320 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-2-Q5.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1862 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-3-Q23.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1504 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-3-Q26.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1646 Nov 19 22:29 T-new-3-Q4.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1524 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-1-Q28.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1496 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-1-Q45.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1351 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-1-Q7.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1413 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-2-Q16.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1608 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-2-Q29.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1501 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-2-Q6.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1541 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-2-Q9.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1379 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q14.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1465 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q23.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1559 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q3.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1589 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q33.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1366 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q37.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1308 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q41.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1450 Nov 19 22:29 T-old-3-Q7.json\n     1\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n     2\t\n     3\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n     4\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n     5\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n     6\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n     7\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n     8\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n     9\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n    10\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n    11\t\n    12\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n    13\t\n    14\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n    17\t2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n    18\t3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n    19\t   word for it is already given.\n    20\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n    21\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n    22\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n    23\t   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n    24\t\n    25\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\n    26\t\n    27\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\n    28\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\n    29\tany one step's own score.\n    30\t\n    31\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n    32\t\n    33\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n    34\t\n    35\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n    36\t\n    37\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n    38\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n    39\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n    40\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n    41\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n    42\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n    43\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n    44\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Evidence:**\n    47\t\n    48\t| Evidence | Content | Source |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n    51\t| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n    52\t| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n    53\t| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n    54\t\n    55\tAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n    56\t\n    57\t## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n    58\t\n    59\t| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n    60\t|---|---|---|\n    61\t| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n    62\t| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n    63\t| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n    64\t| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n    65\t| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n    66\t| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n    67\t| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n    68\t| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n    69\t\n    70\t## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n    71\t\n    72\t- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n    73\t  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n    74\t  system (D263).\n    75\t- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n    76\t  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n    77\t  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n    78\t- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n122:<div class=\"page\">\n123:<nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"目录\">\n126:    <li><a href=\"#decisions\"><span class=\"num\">✓</span>已拍的 12 条</a></li>\n127:    <li><a href=\"#words\"><span class=\"num\">1</span>用词</a></li>\n128:    <li><a href=\"#ledger\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>账本记什么</a></li>\n129:    <li><a href=\"#types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类</a></li>\n130:    <li><a href=\"#opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</a></li>\n131:    <li><a href=\"#evidence\"><span class=\"num\">5</span>证据标准</a></li>\n132:    <li><a href=\"#weight\"><span class=\"num\">6</span>分量</a></li>\n133:    <li><a href=\"#views\"><span class=\"num\">7</span>研究观点</a></li>\n134:    <li><a href=\"#golden\"><span class=\"num\">8</span>金标</a></li>\n135:    <li><a href=\"#method\"><span class=\"num\">9</span>改提示词、测量、迭代</a></li>\n136:    <li><a href=\"#rulings\"><span class=\"num\">10</span>Alex 拍过的</a></li>\n137:    <li><a href=\"#conflicts\"><span class=\"num\">11</span>冲突怎么摆平</a></li>\n138:    <li><a href=\"#checks\"><span class=\"num\">12</span>校验和出处</a></li>\n143:<header class=\"top\">\n144:  <div class=\"eyebrow\">Hivemind · 抽取这一步的 PRD · 第 5 版（第 3 版已签；D248 按 Alex 逐个选的七条修订；D250 证据的四条界线和计数单位）</div>\n146:  <div class=\"status ok\"><span class=\"pill ok\">已签</span><div><b>生效。</b>2026-10-29 Alex 拍了 12 条（D243）；2026-10-30 他逐个选了颗粒度的七条（D248，见\"已拍\"一节），改了第 2、3、4 节，升为第 4 版；2026-10-31 他按我给的倾向定了证据的四条界线和计数单位（D250，见\"已拍\"一节），改了第 5、8、9 节，升为第 5 版。这一页取代第 1 版（<span class=\"path\">docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/standard.md</span>，D229），是抽取这一步唯一的尺子：提示词、金标、回归测量都从它推出。改它要先在 <span class=\"path\">docs/DECISIONS.md</span> 记下 Alex 的原话，再改这一页，再做一次只读的漂移检查。</div></div>\n147:  <div class=\"meta\"><span>2026-10-29 · D241、D242、D243</span><span>分支 fix/extraction-quality-2026-10-28</span><span>起草过程和校验：<span class=\"path\">docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/</span></span></div>\n151:<section class=\"answer\" aria-label=\"一句话\">\n154:  <dd>一个在追这家公司的分析员读到会记进本周笔记的陈述，就留；留下以后另判分量<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2、§4</span>。整体倾向谨慎：杂音很大，不是什么都要抽，不是什么都算线索；但新信息带来的增量要敏感，不能漏<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。预测、传闻、反证、远期、条件情景都可以是证据，不因为\"还没发生\"\"不是官方\"\"离现在远\"\"和我们方向相反\"就不留<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>。有名有姓的动作缺金额、缺日期也照留，分量可以低一点<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。泛泛的主张和背景是常识，没有数字和具体的叙事就不收<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。</dd>\n156:  <dd>一个问题值得单独追，当它的答案可能改变仓位、能在一个日期用公开材料核对、而且库里没有问题在问同一件事<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span>。</dd>\n158:  <dd>一个观点是关于业务和世界的、有论证的看法，它的立场来自论证和市场已经定价的东西相比<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §8</span>。问题当前落在哪一档，由判断这一步按 PRD 06 和 D198 读证据推出。</dd>\n163:<div class=\"tree\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"每句话的去向\">\n164:<ul><li><span class=\"node\">一句话</span>\n166:    <li>在第 5.3 节的不留清单上 <span class=\"goes\">→ 先看那一行的\"边界\"一列：写着\"不能用这一行删掉\"或\"按 5.1 判\"的，按第 5.1 节判，留下的走下面；写着\"要留\"或\"按本来分量\"的照办；写着\"可选\"的归可选；其余不留</span></li>\n167:    <li>分析员会记 <span class=\"goes\">→ 留为证据</span><span class=\"tag\">第 5 节</span>\n169:        <li>记来源层：事实、当事人陈述、第三方观点、传闻 <span class=\"tag\">进账本 · 第 5.5 节</span></li>\n170:        <li>分量：核心、辅助、可选 <span class=\"tag\">只在评估时判，不进账本 · 第 6 节</span></li>\n171:        <li>归档：挂到最窄的那个已开问题 <span class=\"src\">D207</span>；没有问题接，记 no home 扔掉，评估时逐条读 <span class=\"src\">D209</span></li>\n172:        <li>这篇文章还提出了值得追的新问题吗？ <span class=\"tag\">第 4 节</span>\n174:            <li>过了测试，属于五类之一 <span class=\"goes\">→ 候选问题；和库里已有问题是不是重复，由匹配判</span> <span class=\"src\">D211、D190</span></li>\n175:            <li>没过 <span class=\"goes\">→ 不开，它只是证据</span></li>\n184:<h2 id=\"decisions\"><span class=\"num\">已拍</span>Alex 拍板的 12 条</h2>\n190:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n193:<tr><td>1</td><td>分量按信息量定档：核心要碰到关键判断，并带一个量、一个确定状态或一个带期间的预测；别家公司自己的经营数字、对公司是小事的，算辅助；预测离现在越远，越可能只是辅助，由判断定。缺金额、缺日期只影响分到哪一档，不是不留的理由</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 6 节</td></tr>\n194:<tr><td>2</td><td>\"共同量\"按 D191 落实：任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格（合计支出、合约价、利率）都可以开题，开题理由叫 <code>shared_quantity</code>；期间按自然年。提示词和代码要跟着改</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 D 类</td></tr>\n195:<tr><td>3</td><td>生态数字（论文数、获奖、下载量、开发者人数、大会人数）可选</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 6 节</td></tr>\n196:<tr><td>4</td><td>在研公司的估值倍数、市值、孤零零的目标价可选；带推导的条件估值仍是辅助</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 5.3、6 节</td></tr>\n197:<tr><td>5</td><td>典型的主张和背景是常识，没有数字和具体的叙事不收；不是常识的新信息，照第 5.1 节的规则判</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 5.1、5.3 节</td></tr>\n198:<tr><td>6</td><td>旧事重提：重提的过去实际数可选；重提的季度指引和仍然有效的预测、计划按本来分量；文字或日期看不出是旧事的不算重提</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 5.3、6 节</td></tr>\n199:<tr><td>7</td><td>收购算约束性义务（写明规模、尚未完成）</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 C 类</td></tr>\n200:<tr><td>8</td><td>改提示词时的回归判法：全部文章各发一次和上一版比，\"别的版本都留住、只有这一版丢了\"的核心或辅助才算回归信号；它是诊断，验收仍是三次发送</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 9.3 节</td></tr>\n201:<tr><td>9</td><td>来源层：一句话符合两行时取表里上面那行；混合的一条按主要说法定层，次要部分写进摘要</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 5.5 节</td></tr>\n202:<tr><td>10</td><td>只有形容的引语不收</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 5.3 节</td></tr>\n203:<tr><td>11</td><td>金标冻结后发现错：另记一份带理由的更正，写明改前改后，不覆盖原文件；测量用更正后的版本并注明</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 8 节</td></tr>\n204:<tr><td>12</td><td>达标线里\"垃圾\"一项（每篇留下的无关陈述）用定稿金标重算，Luna 基线也重算</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 9.2 节</td></tr>\n210:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n213:<tr><td>1</td><td>同一个计划的几种说法，最后核对同一个数的，是一题；各自会变、会分别盯的数才分开；属于已按金额开题的计划的一笔交易并进去</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n214:<tr><td>2</td><td>同一件事的不同截止日：早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上证据，不等新文章</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n215:<tr><td>3</td><td>同一代产品的几个里程碑：一题，问能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；送样、发布作证据；会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n216:<tr><td>4</td><td>公司自己的量只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n217:<tr><td>5</td><td>事件和政策题里模型写的期间起点，不拿来挡合并</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n218:<tr><td>6</td><td>单笔交易、产品、项目，规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开题；够不上的不开题，它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判，留下的是证据</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 C 类、第 4 节</td></tr>\n219:<tr><td>7</td><td>原始说话人、原始日期、数字都相同的几条证据，代码认作一条，判断时只给看一次、写明几家报道，每条照存；不知道的说话人或日期不算相同</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 2 节</td></tr>\n224:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n227:<tr><td>1</td><td>只描述一个现成安排（合作、客户在用、已有部署）、没有新动作的，是背景，不收，文中没写日期也一样；仍然有效的指引、预测、计划照旧按本来分量</td><td class=\"nowrap\">5.3</td></tr>\n228:<tr><td>2</td><td>别家公司的事，说不出它通过需求、供给、竞争、定价这类路径动了在研公司哪个问题的，不收；只因同一篇文章、同一场活动或同一个生态挨着的，不收</td><td class=\"nowrap\">5.3</td></tr>\n229:<tr><td>3</td><td>公司自己、伙伴或第三方发布的对比是产品细节，不收；只有对手拿来和本公司产品比的按 5.1 判（判例 4 不变）；同一句里伙伴、客户采用或集成的动作不因这一条删，照旧按 5.1 判</td><td class=\"nowrap\">5.3</td></tr>\n230:<tr><td>4</td><td>具名分析师对一件已记下的事的解读，没有新事实或推算的，不收；有新事实或推算的按 5.1 判；条件估值不变</td><td class=\"nowrap\">5.3</td></tr>\n231:<tr><td>5</td><td>计数单位：一条不收的金标条目，只有带着它的那条记录本身不是金标判为核心、辅助或可选的同一件事时，才算留下；引文里顺带带出的不收半句，是那件事的同一条记录</td><td class=\"nowrap\">9.2</td></tr>\n239:<li>标题里的说法和正文是同一条证据，不单记<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2 同一事实的复述</span>。</li>\n244:<h2 id=\"words\"><span class=\"num\">1</span>这一页用的词：一词一义</h2>\n245:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n248:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">陈述</td><td>原文里某一方说的一句话或一件事</td><td></td></tr>\n249:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">证据</td><td>被留下的陈述，带引文、摘要、说话人、原始出处、来源层</td><td>作者的观点（它本身可以是一条证据）</td></tr>\n250:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">问题（观点）</td><td>账本里追踪的一件事：一个问题句、一组结果档、一个到期日，写下后不改<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\n251:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">候选问题</td><td>抽取这一步提议新开的问题</td><td></td></tr>\n252:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">标的问题、主题问题</td><td>标的：答案是一家可交易公司（或币、商品）自己的经营结果。主题：答案是世界上的一件事，影响很多公司<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\n253:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">开题理由</td><td>候选问题值得开的几类理由之一，答案里写在 <code>opens_as</code><span class=\"src\">D184；英文 admission reason</span></td><td></td></tr>\n254:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">结果档</td><td>一个问题事先固定、互不重叠、覆盖全部结果的结局，五档或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 rung</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n255:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">来源层</td><td>事实、当事人陈述、第三方观点、传闻<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 evidence tier</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n256:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">分量</td><td>一条证据对判断有多重要：核心、辅助、可选、不收<span class=\"src\">第 6 节；D243</span>。Alex 说的\"档位低一点\"指它</td><td>结果档、来源层</td></tr>\n257:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究用途</td><td>判断这一步引用一条证据去支持一个具体结论时，它撑得住多强：直接可用、有条件可用、线索、不可用<span class=\"src\">D221，第 7 节</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n258:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">七类驱动</td><td>一条陈述为什么对公司业务重要的七条路径<span class=\"src\">D208</span>。需求：客户要买多少，如订单、客户支出、贷款需求、客流。供给与投入：能做出多少、成本多少，如产能、原料和零部件价格、燃料、矿石品位。竞争与份额：对手的产品、价格、开店、赢单。定价与装机：公司能收多少价、存量多大，如售价、费率、利差、装机量、存量客户。产品周期：发布、出货、试验、获批、延期。政策：法规、许可、关税、利率、监管决定。资本与义务：融资、担保、承诺、投资、收购</td><td>问题类型</td></tr>\n259:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">市场预期与估值</td><td>市场已经定价了什么：估值倍数、市值、目标价、股价反应。观点的立场要和它比<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §8</span>。对一个业务量的一致预期（收入、EPS）是那个业务量的证据，不归这里</td><td>七类驱动</td></tr>\n260:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究组</td><td>几个问题共同在追的一件正在进行的事<span class=\"src\">D165</span></td><td>问题</td></tr>\n263:<h2 id=\"ledger\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>账本里记三种东西</h2>\n264:<ol class=\"steps\">\n265:<li><b>证据</b>一条记录一个陈述，一件事用几句话说仍是一条<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；Alex 判 11</span>。记逐字引文、能单独读懂的一句话摘要、说话人、原始说话人和原始日期（不知道就写不知道，不填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>）、来源层。同一条证据可以挂到几个问题上，推力写在挂接上<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。每一条进来的证据都单独存下；和已有证据的关系（同一说法、修订）由匹配标出，作为意见，两条都留着<span class=\"src\">D202、D204</span>。原始说话人、原始日期、数字都相同的几条（说话人或日期不知道的不算相同），由代码认作同一条：判断时只给看一次，写明几家报道，每条仍照存<span class=\"src\">D248 第 7 条；改 D204 的\"两条都给判断看\"</span>。这条在打开之前要先在同一说法的金标上量两件事（金标按这条规则实际会合的组取，对着原文读）：它会不会藏掉不同或更丰富的说法（比如多一句限定），它依赖的原始说话人、原始日期两个字段准不准；量完之前，照 D204 两条都给判断看。</li>\n266:<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\n267:<li><b>研究组</b>一件正在进行的事（一个产品换代及其部署、一笔融资或收购、一个政策过程、一轮投资或需求周期），把几个问题组织在一起，常常跨公司。它不是问题，也不代替开题判断。公司自己的报表行（收入、毛利率、费用、税率、资本开支）不带研究组，除非这一行本身就在追这样一件事；它也可以加入别的问题建的组<span class=\"src\">D165</span>。</li>\n269:<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\n271:<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n273:<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n276:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n277:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n278:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n279:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n280:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n295:<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n296:<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n297:<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n302:<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n303:<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n304:<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n305:<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n308:<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n309:<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n310:<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n311:<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n313:<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n314:<ol class=\"steps\">\n315:<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n316:<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n318:<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n320:<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n322:<li><b>原文支持：</b>主体、量或事件、时间依据都能在原文找到。原文没给日期、而规则允许研究员定检查日的，用那个日期并标明：没写日期的待决监管事项用本财年末（第 3 节 E 类）；还没签的约束性义务用文章后 18 个月以内能核对签约的那天<span class=\"src\">D185、D210</span>。不把\"拟议\"\"预计\"写成\"已签\"\"已完成\"。</li>\n327:<h3>不开的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 的清单</span></h3>\n328:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n345:<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\n346:<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\n347:<li><b>同一个计划的几种说法</b>（担保、融资承诺、信用支持……），最后核对的是同一个数，是一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。</li>\n348:<li><b>同一件事的不同截止日：</b>早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据，不另开；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上并进来的证据，不等新文章<span class=\"src\">D248 第 2 条</span>。</li>\n349:<li><b>同一代产品的几个里程碑：</b>一题，问能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；送样、发布作证据；会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span>。</li>\n350:<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\n351:<li><b>身份：</b>事件和政策题里模型写的期间起点，不拿来挡合并；对象、事件、截止日照旧核对<span class=\"src\">D248 第 5 条</span>。</li>\n352:<li><b>续期：</b>同一个量或同一串事件的下一个期间<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Succession、D190</span>。</li>\n353:<li><b>另一题：</b>同一件事里答案能分开走、分析员会分别下注的：有自己驱动的组成部分；同一笔交易或同一份附注里两个各自会变、分别盯着的数；另一件事<span class=\"src\">D190 碰撞裁决的四种；D248 第 1 条收窄了\"担保和融资\"</span>。</li>\n354:<li><b>约束性义务：</b>\"一笔或一个计划\"一题<span class=\"src\">D210</span>；一笔交易是不是某个已按金额开题的计划的一部分，由匹配判，是就并入<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。还没签的单笔交易是\"签不签\"的是非题，照旧可以开，不并进计划的金额题<span class=\"src\">D210；PRD 06；D248 未改</span>。</li>\n355:<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\n359:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n363:<tr><td>结果档形状、期间是真日期、到期在文章之后、季度数、年限、约束性义务 18 个月、<code>settled_by</code> 不为空</td><td>代码：只查形状，不判重要性<span class=\"src\">D154、D155、D184</span></td></tr>\n364:<tr><td>和库里的同一题、续期、另一题</td><td>匹配（Jev）和碰撞裁决<span class=\"src\">D190</span>；共同量由代码<span class=\"src\">D197</span></td></tr>\n366:<p class=\"note\">年限按公司财年数：2026 年 7 月时 NVIDIA 在 FY2027（2027 年 1 月结束），所以 FY2028 是明年。代码原来按自然年算，把 FY2028 当成后年拒掉；在 v29 答案的 40 个带年份的候选里拒错了 2 个。已修，测试是 <span class=\"path\">tests/test_fiscal_year_horizon.py</span><span class=\"src\">D243</span>。</p>\n368:<h2 id=\"evidence\"><span class=\"num\">5</span>证据标准</h2>\n370:<blockquote><p><b>一个在追这家公司的分析员，读到会在本周笔记里写下来，因为它让某个问题的答案更可能或更不可能。</b>问题不限于库里已有的，也不限于本公司：客户、供应商、竞争者、监管、宏观都算<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；D208 七类驱动</span>。</p></blockquote>\n371:<p><b>整体倾向谨慎，对增量敏感。</b>杂音很大，不是什么都要抽，不是什么都算线索。判一句话之前先问：这是新信息吗？它让哪个问题的答案变了？一件新发生的事、一个新数字、一个新的具体判断，是增量，不能漏；重复常识、描述长期状况、泛泛的看法，是杂音<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。增量和杂音的具体界线按 5.3 各行和边界一起判<span class=\"src\">D250</span>。</p>\n372:<p>从第一段读到最后一段，分析员会记的（按本节和 5.3 各行边界一起判）都留。一页有八条就是八条，不挑<span class=\"src\">D199</span>。它们通常是下面四类之一；四类描述的是会记的陈述长什么样，不是\"属于四类就一定留\"，留不留由上面的规则判；具体不留的行和边界见 5.3。</p>\n373:<ol class=\"steps\">\n374:<li><b>公司自己的数字、指引或决定</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"同店销售本季增长 4.2%\"；\"管理层把全年收入指引定在 120–130 亿美元\"；\"董事会批准 100 亿美元回购\"；\"公司取消软件订阅费，生产使用免费\"<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 8，Omniverse</span>。</li>\n375:<li><b>客户、供应商、竞争者、伙伴的有规模、有日期或有名字的动作，以及它们公布的数字</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2：三者有一个就够</span>第 1 版的例子\"Google Cloud 季度收入 248 亿美元，增长 82%，积压超过 5000 亿美元\"<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 11</span>；\"最大客户说明年订单砍五分之一\"；\"主要供应商说 2027 年产能翻倍\"；\"对手在欧洲降价 15%\"；\"一家银行选用竞争对手的系统\"；\"一家软件公司把本公司的模型集成进政府系统\"。后两条有名字、没金额，也留<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。</li>\n376:<li><b>具名一方的主张或估计</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"CFO 说十年前建的工厂仍满负荷\"；\"分析师把明年 EPS 预期上调到 4.10 美元\"；\"做空机构指控公司虚增应收 20 亿美元\"；\"内存厂说 2027 年短缺最严重，持续到 2030\"。</li>\n377:<li><b>政策或监管的决定或步骤</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"监管机构批准该药第二个适应症\"；\"政府要求该产品出口须申请许可\"；\"25 家公司联名反对过早限制开放权重模型\"；\"财长说将调查某国公司是否窃取知识产权\"。</li>\n379:<p><b>典型的主张和背景</b><span class=\"src\">D243 第 5 条</span>：Alex 的原话是\"这种典型的主张背景属于常识，基本上抽出来也没有太多的意义除非带数字和具体的叙事不然都是属于不采纳\"。常识，就是跟这家公司的分析员读这篇之前就已经知道的：谁领先、谁在竞争、需求强、供给紧、融资难这类说法，和对已知状况的重述。这类陈述没有数字和具体的叙事就不收。不是常识的，是新信息，比如一份新报告的判断、一个新的市场数据、刚发生的事的细节，照上面的规则判，分析员会记就留。</p>\n387:<p>预测、传闻、反证、远期、条件情景都是证据；它们的层级和确定性另记。不因为\"还没发生\"\"不是官方\"\"离现在远\"\"和我们方向相反\"就不留；一个真实的反例可能比十个顺风数字更重要<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>。有名有姓的动作缺金额、缺日期也是证据，分量可以低一点<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。不留清单只按 5.3 各行和边界删，不能用来删掉标准要留的陈述：\"a reject rule never removes what the standard keeps\"<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。</p>\n389:<h3>5.3 不留的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2 的清单，加 D238、D243 的行</span></h3>\n391:<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n394:<tr><td>没有业务规模的产品、游戏、驱动、跑分细节</td><td>\"这张卡 415W\"；\"Geekbench 跑分\"</td><td>接口、功率、旧型号的支持周期</td><td>对手拿它和本公司产品比的说法不能用这一行删掉，按 5.1 判（Alex 判 4：AMD 2.4 倍是辅助）；伙伴、客户采用或集成的动作不是产品细节（5.1 第 2 类）；公司自己、伙伴或第三方发布的对比（\"比闭源模型便宜 10 倍\"、\"同样功率多放 40% GPU\"、第三方测试）是产品细节，不收；同一句里伙伴、客户采用或集成的动作不因这一条删，照旧按 5.1 判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 3 条</span></td></tr>\n395:<tr><td>股价涨跌、投资人仓位、技术面</td><td>\"本月跌 13%\"；\"Burry 做空\"</td><td>期权成交、基金买卖</td><td>股价反应背后的那条新闻不能用这一行删掉，按 5.1 判；\"财报后股价反应\"可选<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §10.2</span>；在研公司的估值倍数、市值、孤零零的目标价可选<span class=\"src\">D243 第 4 条</span>；别的股价涨跌照旧不留</td></tr>\n396:<tr><td>作者的一般性风险清单和没有推导的看法</td><td>\"如果 AI 退潮会受伤\"</td><td>\"这只股票该持有\"；\"芯片指数是纯粹的高估\"</td><td>有假设、有推导、有时点的条件估值要留<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §10.1</span>；具名分析师对一件已记下的事的解读（\"推迟会给对手留出窗口\"），没有新事实或推算的，不收，有新事实或推算的按 5.1 判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 4 条</span></td></tr>\n397:<tr><td>记者的背景和框架</td><td>\"A100 2020 年上市\"；\"海湾国家花了几十亿但仍依赖它\"</td><td>\"公司成立于 1998 年\"；通用的技术讲解</td><td>没有数字和具体叙事的主张和背景不收；怎么分见 5.1<span class=\"src\">D243 第 5 条</span>；只描述一个现成安排（合作、客户在用、已有部署）、没有新动作的，是背景，不收，文中没写日期也一样<span class=\"src\">D250 第 1 条</span></td></tr>\n400:<tr><td>已知事实的重述</td><td>两个月后再说一遍 Q1 收入、指引、已公布的回购</td><td></td><td>抽取看不到库，只能从文字和日期看。重提的过去实际数可选；重提的季度指引和仍然有效的预测、计划按本来分量；看不出是旧事的不算重提<span class=\"src\">D243 第 6 条</span>；只描述现成安排、没有新动作的，按背景判（见\"记者的背景和框架\"一行），其余仍按这一行判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 1 条</span></td></tr>\n402:<tr><td>只有形容的引语</td><td></td><td>\"a pivotal moment\"；\"heterogeneous inference\"（role-v18 原文的例子）</td><td><span class=\"src\">D243 第 10 条</span></td></tr>\n403:<tr><td>新加坡转运案件的概况和被告个人资产</td><td></td><td></td><td>可选，收不收都不扣分<span class=\"src\">D231</span></td></tr>\n405:<p>另外一条来自后来的决定：<b>和公司所有市场都无关的别家公司的估值、股价、交易</b>不留（D238：\"another company's valuation, share price or deals that touch none of the company's markets\"）。别家公司的动作和经营数字不能用这一行删掉，它们留不留按 5.1 的规则判：要说得出它通过需求、供给、竞争、定价这类路径动了在研公司的哪个问题；只因同一篇文章、同一场活动或同一个生态挨着、说不出这条路径的，不收<span class=\"src\">D250 第 2 条</span>。</p>\n408:<h3>5.4 一条记录必须保住的意思<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，原样</span></h3>\n409:<p>六格里只填这一条用得上的<span class=\"src\">D220</span>。</p>\n410:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n416:<tr><td>哪个期间</td><td>预测或事实覆盖的期间；\"今年\"按公司财年或自然年写都算对<span class=\"src\">D233</span>，余下时间不改成全年</td><td>\"今年余下时间\"改成 FY2027 全年</td></tr>\n420:<p>原始发言日不知道就写不知道，不能填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>。一条记录单独读要能懂，条件不能只放在旁边另一条里<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，引主分支 D251；两个分支的决定编号各自独立，D227</span>。不必要的：转述机构、普通发言场合、付费方案全名；漏了不扣原意分，<b>编造了仍算记录错误</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3</span>。没有来源证实的结论，可以作为分析员的推断写出，但不能写成来源说的事实<span class=\"src\">D218</span>。</p>\n421:<p>边界<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>：Sharon 合同是供需的辅助证据，不是担保金额的证据；NVL72x2 取消归产品进度<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 10</span>。</p>\n423:<h3>5.5 来源层<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 的四层；D238 采纳的 role-v29 原文</span></h3>\n426:<p>这两处列了四层，下表把它们排成一张。一句话同时符合两行时，取表里上面那行<span class=\"src\">D243 第 9 条</span>。</p>\n427:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n436:<p>一条记录里既有已发生的部分、又有计划或传闻的细节，按主要说法定层，次要部分的性质写进摘要；不拆成两条，除非是两件事<span class=\"src\">D243 第 9 条</span>。层级之间的关系：后来的确认和先前的传闻都留在账本里；匹配判断两条的关系（同一说法、修订或新的），修订的条件过了才记修订，没过就作为新的一条存下<span class=\"src\">D202、D204</span>；同一说法在判断时怎么显示，见第 2 节<span class=\"src\">D248 第 7 条</span>；判断时只有事实能确定到期落在哪一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。</p>\n438:<h2 id=\"weight\"><span class=\"num\">6</span>分量</h2>\n439:<p>分量问\"这条对判断多重要\"，分四级。按投资后果判它碰到的是什么；核心和辅助的界线按信息量定<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §4；D243 第 1 条</span>。缺金额、缺日期只影响分到哪一档，不是不留的理由<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。分量不由数字多不多、是不是官方、库里有没有页、和我们方向是否相同、文章篇幅决定<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §4</span>；离现在远不是不留的理由<span class=\"src\">D216</span>，它落在核心还是辅助由判断定。</p>\n440:<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n443:<tr><td><span class=\"w core\">核心</span></td><td>碰到关键判断，并且带着能定位答案的信息。关键判断：收入、利润、融资或信用风险、需求、关键产品进度、关键投入的供给和价格；相对在研公司判，包括它的约束性义务和它承载价值的那一代产品及其配置、过渡方案。能定位答案的信息：一个量（金额、比例、数量；在谈的金额也算，\"在谈\"写进意思里）、一个确定状态，或一个带期间的预测。对公司不是小事，也不是别家公司自己的经营数字</td><td>分析师预计今年余下收入增长 82%、2027 年 41%；云巨头 2026 年合计支出 6500 亿美元；内存厂说短缺持续到 2030；为客户 1050 亿美元租约担保；公司宣布为云客户产能兜底的新计划（确定状态，没给金额）；银行指引全年净利息收入降 3–5%；监管机构批准主力药或定下裁决日；主要供应商宣布 9 月起涨价 8%；交易对手披露公司 34 亿美元的采购承诺；据报道在谈最多 6000 亿美元的支持</td></tr>\n444:<tr><td><span class=\"w sup\">辅助</span></td><td>支持或反驳上面的判断，或给出可检验的估值假设；碰到关键判断但没有能定位答案的信息；别家公司自己的经营数字（收入、利润率、积压订单）；对公司规模来说是小事的；离现在越远、判断下来只是辅助的预测</td><td>对手自己模拟的 2.4 倍性能比较；公司取消软件订阅费；三条开放模型政策表态；Sharon 六年 72 MW 合同；FY2028 EPS 一致预期；12.76 × 25 的条件估值；一家银行选用对手系统（没写金额）；伙伴把公司模型集成进政府系统（没写金额）；内存厂公布的季度收入和利润率；客户公布的订单积压；客户园区\"规划最多 17 万颗 GPU\"</td></tr>\n445:<tr><td><span class=\"w opt\">可选</span></td><td>帮助理解市场预期，省略不损害论证；留不留都不扣分</td><td>财报后股价反应；在研公司的估值倍数、市值、孤零零的目标价；生态数字；重提的过去实际数；新加坡案件<span class=\"src\">D231、D243 第 3、4、6 条</span></td></tr>\n446:<tr><td><span class=\"w exc\">不收</span></td><td>第 5.3 节的各行；与判断无关</td><td>模板；产品参数；个人仓位；空泛风险；没有数字和具体叙事的主张</td></tr>\n450:<ol class=\"steps\">\n452:<li><b>是可选的那几样吗？</b>在研公司的估值倍数、市值、孤零零的目标价，财报后股价反应，生态数字，重提的过去实际数，新加坡案件，归可选。带推导的条件估值例外，是辅助<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §10.1</span>。</li>\n456:<p><b>Alex 拍过的分量</b><span class=\"src\">D215；gold-check.md，D229</span>：收入增速核心；内存短缺核心；AMD 跑分辅助；三条政策辅助；云厂商支出核心；Omniverse 辅助；Sharon \"辅助属于供给需求\"；商谈最多 6000 亿支持 OpenAI 核心（在谈的金额）；投资 SB Energy 15 亿核心；Broadcom AI 半导体收入 +143%、Google Cloud 三个数辅助（别家公司的经营数字）；FY2028 EPS 辅助（远期）；逐案审核、有拒绝辅助（没有量和确定结果）。</p>\n457:<p><b>分量只在评估时判。</b>分量只在金标和测量里判，不进账本，不进抽取的输出<span class=\"src\">D240</span>；账本只存来源层。抽取的模型决定留不留、怎么写，以及提哪些候选问题<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §1</span>。</p>\n458:<p>仿真里剩下的分歧几乎都在核心和辅助这条线上：\"对公司规模来说是不是小事\"从一句话里常常看不出来（第 12 节，第三轮）。所以核心和辅助分开报，评估时允许读者间合理的不同判<span class=\"src\">D226、D228</span>。</p>\n460:<h2 id=\"views\"><span class=\"num\">7</span>研究观点标准</h2>\n463:<li><b>观点是什么：</b>一个关于业务和世界的、有论证的看法；立场来自论证和市场已经定价的东西相比；报表行是它的证据，不是它的定义<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §8</span>。</li>\n464:<li><b>判断读什么：</b>一个问题的判断看到的，是它仍然有效的证据里的两部分：新到的（在它倒数第五次判断之后挂上的；判断不满五次时全部显示）和依据（最近十次判断里被引用过的）。其余仍在账本里有效，请求里写明还有多少条没显示；答案只能引用和推动显示了的<span class=\"src\">D198；从 judging-v5 起，v4 的配置照旧读全部有效证据</span>。依赖问题的结论和理由、标的问题的主题块也读<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D195</span>。主题结论变了，同一轮里排队重判符合条件的标的问题；主题的结论不作为证据引用<span class=\"src\">D195</span>。</li>\n465:<li><b>研究的交付物是论证：</b>保留不可改的来源记录，和一份有版本的研究论证，写明支持和反对的来源、是否独立、变化和局限<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</li>\n466:<li><b>研究用途：</b>评估判断时，读者按四级看它引用的每条证据对那个具体结论撑得住多强：直接可用、有条件可用、线索、不可用；同一条证据对不同结论可以不同<span class=\"src\">D221</span>。这是评估的读法，不是判断这一步要输出或存下的字段（D221：\"not a numerical confidence score or a new storage layer\"）。用途和分量不同：分量问\"这条多重要\"，用途问\"拿它证明这个结论够不够\"。</li>\n467:<li><b>事实和推断分开：</b>来源没说的结论可以作为分析员推断写出，但要标明<span class=\"src\">D218</span>。只有事实能确定落在哪一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。</li>\n468:<li><b>重复不是新证据，模型意见一致不是互相印证</b><span class=\"src\">AGENTS §8</span>。</li>\n471:<h2 id=\"golden\"><span class=\"num\">8</span>金标：改提示词的测试标准</h2>\n472:<p class=\"note\">下面这份第 3 版金标是历史记录。第 4 版（D248）改了开题的规则，没有改动证据条目（逐条核对见 <span class=\"path\">research/2026-10-30-noise/gold-v4-evidence-check.md</span>）；第 5 版（D250）改了证据的四条界线。金标的证据部分按第 5 版重推，两位互不知情的读者逐条判，分歧对着原文定，另存成新文件冻结，每条改动写改前、改后和理由，第 3 版文件不动（D243 第 11 条）。开题部分要按第 4 版逐条重判，重判之前打分程序不报开题的分；证据部分版本对不上，打分程序拒绝打分（D244、D250）。</p>\n473:<p class=\"note\">第 5 版金标（2026-10-31 冻结）：<span class=\"path\">docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/golden-v5-dev.json</span>（sha256 <code>6f9476bb6a81ea590af273a71565e7c3c0f49908d26274b8482d52cfdee31a21</code>）和 <span class=\"path\">golden-v5-test.json</span>（sha256 <code>af2145cdc60c34ec1ded0bebcb809800e187d616992ea325919c3ad771da61e3</code>）。重判了 537 条（全部要收、可收的证据，引 D238、别家公司、5.1 判断或新加坡案件的不收句，和盲读认为该留的 35 句）：Codex 和 Claude 两位读者各自盲读，96 条进裁定，62 处改动逐条写改前、改后、两位读者的判法和理由（<span class=\"path\">golden-v5/corrections-v5.json</span>）。开发集：核心 86（不变）、辅助 151（原 181）、可选 72；不收 770、可选 31。测试集：核心 9、辅助 37（原 42）、可选 1。两篇以中东冲突主题为对象的文章，读者被告知按在研公司读，是说明写错，那几条不改。下面的数字是第 3 版的历史记录。</p>\n474:<p>按这一页从原文逐篇写的参照，用来量提示词改动。Alex 的要求是\"以上有你自己trace 过的golden set 来做为改prompt测试标准\"<span class=\"src\">D241</span>。定稿文件：<span class=\"path\">docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json</span>，sha256 <code>78844bc329fc85000e18ddcab9ea59feb57abe6407cf11bbead4ba8fe4c3c0d3</code><span class=\"src\">D243</span>。</p>\n475:<div class=\"tiles\">\n476:<div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"v\">118</div><div class=\"l\">篇测试文章：那一周 98 篇，留出 20 篇</div></div>\n477:<div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"v\">348</div><div class=\"l\">条要收或可以收的证据，一件事一条</div></div>\n478:<div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"v\">738</div><div class=\"l\">句不收，各写理由；另有 24 句可选</div></div>\n479:<div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"v\">1110</div><div class=\"l\">段原文片段，代码核过都在原文里</div></div>\n480:<div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"v\">28 · 42</div><div class=\"l\">个必须开、可以开的问题；240 个不该开</div></div>\n492:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n493:<thead><tr><th>那一组</th><th class=\"num-cell\">核心</th><th class=\"num-cell\">辅助</th><th class=\"num-cell\">可选</th><th class=\"num-cell\">要收或可收</th><th class=\"num-cell\">不收</th><th class=\"num-cell\">原列不收、现为可选</th></tr></thead>\n495:<tr><td>那一周 98 篇</td><td class=\"num-cell\">80</td><td class=\"num-cell\">152</td><td class=\"num-cell\">63</td><td class=\"num-cell\">295</td><td class=\"num-cell\">621</td><td class=\"num-cell\">22</td></tr>\n496:<tr><td>留出 20 篇</td><td class=\"num-cell\">6</td><td class=\"num-cell\">29</td><td class=\"num-cell\">18</td><td class=\"num-cell\">53</td><td class=\"num-cell\">117</td><td class=\"num-cell\">2</td></tr>\n501:<ol class=\"steps\">\n503:<li><b>合并时统一写法</b><span class=\"path\">merge.py</span> 统一各批的写法，每处写理由（<span class=\"path\">merge-log.txt</span>）：旧事重提 49 条逐条判；估值倍数和别家公司股价按现行规则处理；中国是否批准 H200 进口改为主题问题。</li>\n505:<li><b>两轮独立盲读</b>Codex 读者只读这份标准和原文，不看金标。读者多留的逐条对原文判：金标漏了的补上，其余写明不补的理由。补进来的 49 条，\"谁\"和\"意思\"对着原文补齐（<span class=\"path\">additions-fields.json</span>）。</li>\n506:<li><b>按签字定稿</b><span class=\"path\">finalize.py</span> 按 D243 给每一条定分量，39 处改动逐条写理由（<span class=\"path\">finalize-log.txt</span>）：32 条移出要收的一栏，其中 24 条是常识性的主张和背景（第 5 条），1 条是只有形容的引语（第 10 条），7 条和起草者写了理由的不收句是同一句；另有 7 句不收句和要收的条目重复，删掉。这 19 处\"同一句话既留又不留\"，是盲读后补条目时没和不收的句子对照造成的。此外，不收的句子里 24 句按第 3、4、6 条改为可选。</li>\n508:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n509:<thead><tr><th>盲读</th><th class=\"num-cell\">金标条目</th><th class=\"num-cell\">读者也留了</th><th class=\"num-cell\">分量相同</th><th class=\"num-cell\">读者多留</th><th class=\"num-cell\">补进金标</th></tr></thead>\n511:<tr><td>第一轮：随机 15 篇，补之前</td><td class=\"num-cell\">34</td><td class=\"num-cell\">33</td><td class=\"num-cell\">26</td><td class=\"num-cell\">19</td><td class=\"num-cell\">8</td></tr>\n512:<tr><td>第一轮：补之后</td><td class=\"num-cell\">42</td><td class=\"num-cell\">41</td><td class=\"num-cell\">32</td><td class=\"num-cell\">11</td><td class=\"num-cell\"></td></tr>\n513:<tr><td>第二轮：其余 103 篇，补之前</td><td class=\"num-cell\">229</td><td class=\"num-cell\">194</td><td class=\"num-cell\">162</td><td class=\"num-cell\">144</td><td class=\"num-cell\">40</td></tr>\n514:<tr><td>第二轮：补之后</td><td class=\"num-cell\">262</td><td class=\"num-cell\">227</td><td class=\"num-cell\">193</td><td class=\"num-cell\"></td><td class=\"num-cell\"></td></tr>\n516:<p>结论：起草稿大约漏了两成，集中在有名有姓、没写规模的采用和合作，和一些带期间的判断。补完以后，独立读者能找到的金标条目约九成。读者多留的 163 条里，48 条是金标漏了、已补；其余 115 条按标准不补：同一件事金标已有、新加坡案件、产品细节、泛泛看法、旧事重提、合作方自己的事、和公司市场无关、只描述长期状况。剩下的不一致集中在核心和辅助的界线（第 1 条）和\"背景还是主张\"（第 5 条），两条都已由 Alex 拍定。记录在 <span class=\"path\">golden-v3/spotcheck.md</span>、<span class=\"path\">pass2-decisions.json</span>。</p>\n522:<li><b>发现错了怎么办。</b>不改这个文件；另记一份更正，每条写理由和改前改后，测量用更正后的版本并注明<span class=\"src\">D243 第 11 条</span>。</li>\n526:<h2 id=\"method\"><span class=\"num\">9</span>改提示词、测量、迭代</h2>\n527:<p class=\"note\">签字以后的第一件事：把现行提示词（role-v29）和这一页逐句对一遍，列出不一致的地方，再按 9.3 一类一类改。一般的规则全文在 <span class=\"path\">AGENTS.md</span> §6（写提示词）和 §7（测量和迭代），这里只写到这一步怎么用，出处标在后面。</p>\n531:<li><b>每一句都对得上这一页。</b>提示词里每一句关于留、不留、分量、开题的话，在这一页找得到出处；找不到的，是给 Alex 的提议，不是改动<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §6</span>。</li>\n532:<li><b>写\"不留\"之前先核它删不掉要留的。</b>分析员会记的陈述，缺金额、缺日期本身不是不留的理由；分量另判，可能低一点<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。Alex 的原话：\"我不是和你说过不要这么死板吗？……你应该把它记录下来，只是可能档位低一点\"。</li>\n533:<li><b>通用的对冲基金大脑。</b>每一句、每个例子对银行、药企、零售、芯片读起来一样；例子跨行业，不点名覆盖的公司，不取自测试文章<span class=\"src\">D237；AGENTS §6</span>。</li>\n534:<li><b>不靠加长。</b>读整个请求，就像模型读到的那样（系统提示、schema、内容）；列出矛盾、为别的情况写的规则、逼出缺陷的说法；删、并、拆。缺一句才加，别处删掉同样多；报改前改后的字数和 token<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §6</span>。</li>\n535:<li><b>分类写成封闭集合。</b>每类两三个跨行业的例子，加走法（从第一段读到最后一段）和停止点（\"一页有八条就是八条\"）<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §6</span>。例子就是指令：和 schema、读答案的代码不一致的例子删掉。</li>\n536:<li><b>发之前先免费核一遍。</b>写一份照提示词作答的假答案，过一遍全部代码检查；契约句逐条对金标该收和该拒的例子读一遍；确认发出去的字节和生产一样；<span class=\"path\">scripts/preflight.py</span> 把存下的答案重放一遍<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §5、§6</span>。</li>\n541:<li><b>一把尺子。</b>这一页 → 定稿金标 → 下面的达标线。另一把尺子在用，比如旧参考答案、评审打分表、提示词自己的类别，就是缺陷，先修掉再测<span class=\"src\">D241；AGENTS §7</span>。</li>\n542:<li><b>计数单位。</b>一条\"不收\"的金标条目，只有带着它的那条记录本身不是金标判为核心、辅助或可选的同一件事时，才算留下；引文里顺带带出的不收半句，是那件事的同一条记录，不算误收。是不是同一件事，代码的计数辅助先算，有出入的由读者对着原文判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 5 条；第 2 节\"一件事用几句话说仍是一条\"</span>。</li>\n543:<li><b>不在还在改的尺子上给自己打分。</b>金标先给 Alex 看、冻结，再开始改提示词；意思由没写这次改动的读者按金标判；代码只核结构和计数<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §7</span>。</li>\n544:<li><b>被扔的逐条读。</b>按四种归因计数（第 2 节），从最大的一类修起<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。</li>\n545:<li><b>总数只看三次发送。</b>一次发送只能说明机制；直接读（每篇发一次，每个答案和原文并排读，D238）用来找机制，它的数是一次发送的数，要这样标明。回归先报，每个数都报<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §7</span>。</li>\n563:<p>引文检查接受的写法：只在标点、引号、大小写上和原文不同，或在一句之内省略一段，存原文<span class=\"src\">D236</span>。</p>\n564:<p>之后的决定对它的影响：参考答案第 2 版里\"整篇什么都不留\"的标注不再当目标<span class=\"src\">D240</span>；\"垃圾\"一项用定稿金标重算，Luna 基线也重算<span class=\"src\">D243 第 12 条</span>；第 1 版说的\"§6 例子里该开的一个问题\"是 AI Compute Partnership 的义务金额题；合理的不同判和不同措辞可以接受，可选细节和标签不同不变成硬性的过或不过<span class=\"src\">D226、D228</span>。</p>\n568:<ol class=\"steps\">\n569:<li><b>挑最大的一类</b>把漏收、误收和被扔的按机制归类计数，从最大的一类开始；报这一类占多少<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §1</span>。</li>\n570:<li><b>找到是哪一句</b>读这一类的原始答案，和原文并排（改之前一共至少读过十个原始答案）；对模型做出的选择，接着那次对话问它\"哪一句让你这样判\"；先看请求里有没有它需要的、schema 写不写得出<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §1、§6</span>。</li>\n571:<li><b>只改一处</b>一次改一句或一组说同一件事的话，别处删掉同样多；新的话对得上这一页<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §6</span>。</li>\n572:<li><b>全部文章各发一次，和上一版比</b>改一句会改变每一次请求，所以要发的是全部文章。\"别的版本都留住、只有这一版丢了\"的核心或辅助才算回归信号；单次发送本身每版有 0–4 条这样的意外丢失<span class=\"src\">D243 第 8 条；surprise.py</span>。每个信号读原始答案、问模型自己的理由，追到是不是这次改的那一句造成的。这是诊断。出错的那几篇只用来找机制；接不接受，看全部文章三次发送、和新对照一起报的结果<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §7</span>。</li>\n573:<li><b>记一行</b>假设、改动、数字（回归先报）、留不留；没用的改动和自己的错也记<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §7</span>。</li>\n574:<li><b>一批改完再验收</b>在最终配置上三次发送，按 9.2 由不是作者的读者评，结果给 Alex<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §11</span>。</li>\n576:<p class=\"note warn\"><b>尺子有疑问就停。</b>改的时候发现金标和这一页说法不同、两份标准打架、或读者对\"什么是对的\"有分歧，就停下来先和 Alex 定尺子，不在有疑问的尺子上接着调<span class=\"src\">D241；AGENTS §7</span>。</p>\n578:<h2 id=\"rulings\"><span class=\"num\">10</span>Alex 已经拍过的判例</h2>\n580:<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n583:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-22</td><td class=\"nowrap\">讲话方式</td><td>\"explain and answer like I'm 16 and in human understandable language\"</td></tr>\n584:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">AGENTS §8</td><td class=\"nowrap\">观点是什么</td><td>A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument weighed against what is priced. Financial-statement lines are its evidence, never its definition.</td></tr>\n585:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-26 D191</td><td class=\"nowrap\">共同量、主题</td><td>决定文字：\"<code>industry_aggregate</code> is renamed <code>shared_quantity</code>: a quantity or price outside any one company that several move on\"，Alex：\"好\"；纯宏观文章只在主题在名单上时开，Alex：\"是\"；主题对公司一对全部，Alex：\"我觉得这个 1 to all mapping 比较 make sense\"</td></tr>\n586:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-26 D187</td><td class=\"nowrap\">别家公司的量</td><td>选 C（\"可以\"）：任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算；记录，未实现</td></tr>\n587:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-27</td><td class=\"nowrap\">这一步的标准</td><td>\"做一个 hedge fund analyst 的专业视角去看怎么做这一步的标准\"；\"什么叫重要陈述，你也没给例子\"</td></tr>\n588:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-28 D208</td><td class=\"nowrap\">驱动层</td><td>\"可以，但是不能因为有了这层我们的抽取就是非常的模版化缺少了hedge fund analyst 的灵魂\"；宏观\"算是个global factor to all, 但影响正反面不一定\"</td></tr>\n589:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-28 D209</td><td class=\"nowrap\">没家的陈述</td><td>\"if it doesn't matter, just fucking throw it away … if there are false positives that got thrown away … you got to pick it up. Again, that's the way to do proper evaluation.\"</td></tr>\n590:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-28</td><td class=\"nowrap\">不许前视</td><td>\"不是你这么粗暴的把这些都先写好那岂不是lookahead了\"</td></tr>\n591:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-28</td><td class=\"nowrap\">逐条读</td><td>\"有用的，你得一条一条看是不是真的值得抽才知道你这些改动的抽取效果\"</td></tr>\n592:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D215</td><td class=\"nowrap\">十一题</td><td>1 A（收入增速 核心）；2 C→D216 \"2028 EPS 预测可以留下来啊，我的意思是因为太久远了，现在才2026\"；3 A（内存短缺 核心）；4 B（AMD 跑分 辅助）；5 C（新加坡案件 不留，D231 改为可选）；6 B（三条政策 辅助）；7 A（云厂商支出 核心）；8 B（Omniverse 辅助）；9 \"辅助属于供给需求\"（Sharon）；10 \"属于产品进度问题\"（NVL72x2）；11 \"一条吧都属于财务\"（Google Cloud 三个数一条）</td></tr>\n593:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D218</td><td class=\"nowrap\">推断</td><td>\"是推断，你不要再问我了，你要自己尝试 figure out 开始跑\"</td></tr>\n594:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D220</td><td class=\"nowrap\">谁定标准</td><td>\"你来修正对齐，你是 hedge fund analyst 你来做好标准\"</td></tr>\n595:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D217</td><td class=\"nowrap\">目标模型</td><td>\"现在开始以haiku 为模型取代luna … 每一轮都根据尺子去迭代 … 小心 overfit … 尺子其实不对 … scope creep\"（D234 起 Haiku 暂停）</td></tr>\n596:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D226、D228</td><td class=\"nowrap\">评法</td><td>合理的模糊和不同措辞可以接受；金标例子教的是判断逻辑，不是唯一答案；两套既有标准（证据层次、90 题评审）都要用；来源、用途、准入分开判</td></tr>\n597:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29</td><td class=\"nowrap\">今天</td><td>\"之前没有对齐一个hedge fund analyst 应该要用什么标准来抽研究观点\"</td></tr>\n598:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D229</td><td class=\"nowrap\">标准不漂移</td><td>\"1-5 都可以，按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"</td></tr>\n599:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D231</td><td class=\"nowrap\">新加坡</td><td>\"新加坡那条就随意吧\"</td></tr>\n600:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D233</td><td class=\"nowrap\">今年</td><td>按公司财年或自然年写都算对</td></tr>\n601:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D236</td><td class=\"nowrap\">三条提议</td><td>\"好都按照你的提议来。但是你的prompt 改动要确认不是hardcode for nvidia 你在建构的是hedge fund brain\"</td></tr>\n602:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D237</td><td class=\"nowrap\">通用</td><td>\"It needs to be general purpose as a hedge fund brain\"</td></tr>\n603:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D238</td><td class=\"nowrap\">直接读</td><td>\"你根本不要再给我跑什么三轮了。每一篇的问题明显地出错的你不要再用工具尺子了，你直接下去看\"</td></tr>\n604:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D240</td><td class=\"nowrap\">不完整的证据</td><td>\"我不是和你说过不要这么死板吗？这个证据显然是有意义的，不一定什么条件数据时间都要满足，你应该把它记录下来，只是可能档位低一点\"</td></tr>\n605:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D241</td><td class=\"nowrap\">这份标准</td><td>\"几个大类型的账本 - 开题标准和档次 这两个要完整的定义好写好\"；\"档位根据信息量作定标 -以上有你自己trace 过的golden set 来做为改prompt测试标准\"</td></tr>\n606:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D243</td><td class=\"nowrap\">签字</td><td>第 5 条：\"这种典型的主张背景属于常识，基本上抽出来也没有太多的意义除非带数字和具体的叙事不然都是属于不采纳\"；方向：\"不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过\"；\"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"</td></tr>\n607:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D242</td><td class=\"nowrap\">这一页</td><td>\"你给我一个网页，这个同时也是你这个环节重要的PRD\"</td></tr>\n608:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-30 D248</td><td class=\"nowrap\">颗粒度</td><td>七条各选 A（第 6 条\"A， A\"）；原则：\"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\"</td></tr>\n611:<h2 id=\"conflicts\"><span class=\"num\">11</span>在用的标准之间的冲突，怎么摆平</h2>\n612:<p>编号对应盘点报告 <span class=\"path\">inventory-2026-10-29.md</span> 的 B1–B20，B21 是后来加的。\"按已拍的\"是已有决定，只是没落实或没写全；文首 12 条的决定记在 D243；\"我定\"只限措辞和记录约定。</p>\n613:<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n632:<tr><td>B17</td><td>代码按自然年拒公司明年的财年量</td><td>已修：年限按公司财年数，测试 <span class=\"path\">tests/test_fiscal_year_horizon.py</span></td><td>PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；D243</td></tr>\n639:<h2 id=\"checks\"><span class=\"num\">12</span>校验记录和出处</h2>\n642:<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n643:<thead><tr><th>第三轮，一对读者</th><th class=\"num-cell\">新案例：留不留</th><th class=\"num-cell\">新案例：连分量</th><th class=\"num-cell\">难案例复核：留不留</th><th class=\"num-cell\">新问题</th></tr></thead>\n645:<tr><td>作者–Codex</td><td class=\"num-cell\">96%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">87%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">84%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">5/8</td></tr>\n646:<tr><td>作者–Claude sonnet</td><td class=\"num-cell\">94%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">83%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">91%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">6/8</td></tr>\n647:<tr><td>作者–Claude fable</td><td class=\"num-cell\">93%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">81%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">89%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">6/8</td></tr>\n648:<tr><td>Codex–sonnet</td><td class=\"num-cell\">94%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">83%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">86%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">7/8</td></tr>\n649:<tr><td>Codex–fable</td><td class=\"num-cell\">93%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">83%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">84%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">7/8</td></tr>\n650:<tr><td>sonnet–fable</td><td class=\"num-cell\">98%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">89%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">95%</td><td class=\"num-cell\">8/8</td></tr>\n652:<p>新案例上留不留的一致率从第二轮的 80–94% 升到 93–98%，连分量从 72–87% 升到 81–89%。剩下的分歧几乎都在核心和辅助的界线，由 D243 第 1 条定下判法。三位读者判对、作者判错的，记作作者的错：最大客户带来的收入和中国销售占比不该开题（独立意义测试），还有两处陈述。记录在 <span class=\"path\">simulation-log.md</span>。</p>\n656:<div class=\"chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"每一轮漂移检查的发现数：36、约20、约10、6、8、7、7、6、5、6、5\">\n658:<line class=\"axis\" x1=\"28\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"548\" y2=\"170\"/>\n660:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"36\" y=\"44\" width=\"34\" height=\"126\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"53\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\">36</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.3</text>\n661:<rect class=\"bar approx\" x=\"82\" y=\"100\" width=\"34\" height=\"70\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"99\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"middle\">约20</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.4</text>\n662:<rect class=\"bar approx\" x=\"128\" y=\"135\" width=\"34\" height=\"35\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"145\" y=\"129\" text-anchor=\"middle\">约10</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.5</text>\n663:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"174\" y=\"149\" width=\"34\" height=\"21\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"191\" y=\"143\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.6</text>\n664:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"220\" y=\"142\" width=\"34\" height=\"28\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"237\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><text x=\"237\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.7</text>\n665:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"266\" y=\"145.5\" width=\"34\" height=\"24.5\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"283\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><text x=\"283\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.8</text>\n666:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"312\" y=\"145.5\" width=\"34\" height=\"24.5\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"329\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.9</text>\n667:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"358\" y=\"149\" width=\"34\" height=\"21\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"375\" y=\"143\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"375\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.10</text>\n668:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"404\" y=\"152.5\" width=\"34\" height=\"17.5\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"421\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.11</text>\n669:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"450\" y=\"149\" width=\"34\" height=\"21\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"467\" y=\"143\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"467\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.12</text>\n670:<rect class=\"bar\" x=\"496\" y=\"152.5\" width=\"34\" height=\"17.5\"/><text class=\"val\" x=\"513\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"513\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.13</text>\n677:<p>PRD 06（Two thesis kinds、Ladder、Four evidence tiers、State、Succession）；PRD 05；第 1 版标准（D229）；<span class=\"path\">research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/codex-challenger.md</span> §1 八条和 §6、<span class=\"path\">industry-debate-standards.md</span>（主分支）；决定 D155、D165、D184、D185、D186、D187、D190、D191、D195、D197、D198、D199、D201、D202、D204、D207、D208、D209、D210、D211、D215、D216、D218、D220、D221、D226、D228、D229、D231、D233、D236、D237、D238、D240、D241、D242。</p>\n681:<li>这一页：<span class=\"path\">docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html</span>。改它之前先在 <span class=\"path\">docs/DECISIONS.md</span> 记下 Alex 的原话；改完跑一次只读的漂移检查。</li>\n682:<li>起草过程和证据：<span class=\"path\">docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/</span>：<span class=\"path\">standard-v2.md</span> 到 <span class=\"path\">standard-v2.14.md</span>、<span class=\"path\">simulation-log.md</span>、<span class=\"path\">review-drift-v2.*.md</span>、<span class=\"path\">inventory-2026-10-29.md</span>、<span class=\"path\">golden-v3/</span>。</li>\n683:<li>定稿金标：<span class=\"path\">golden-v3/golden-v3-signed.json</span>（sha256 见第 8 节），由 <span class=\"path\">golden-v3/finalize.py</span> 从起草稿定稿。</li>\n684:<li>第 1 版：<span class=\"path\">docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/standard.md</span>（D229），已由这一页取代，留作出处。</li>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path; import json; [(lambda d: print(p.stem, d.get(\\\"account\\\", d)))(json.loads(p.read_text())) for p in sorted(Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account\\\").glob(\\\"*.json\\\"))]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path; import json; [(lambda d: print(p.stem, d.get(\\\"account\\\", d)))(json.loads(p.read_text())) for p in sorted(Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account\\\").glob(\\\"*.json\\\"))]'\"","aggregated_output":"T-new-2-Q11 “The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.”\n\nI weighed these two statements least:\n\n- **e1181:** “At least a dozen other U.S. states have proposed legislation similar to New York's restriction.” Proposals indicate political momentum, but the question counts enacted measures, not proposals.\n- **e3714:** “Texas has frozen new grid connections while officials audit data-center developers.” This signals constraint, but does not establish an enacted construction moratorium or other qualifying state restriction.\nT-new-2-Q20 The instruction was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed least SoftBank’s planned ¥1 trillion retail bond sale (e2315): it is not yet issued and does not establish how much qualifies as AI-infrastructure investment-grade issuance. I also did not add NVIDIA’s $25 billion general-purpose debt issue (e2806) separately to S&P’s broader tally: the evidence does not establish that the whole issue funds AI infrastructure, or that it is outside the tally.\nT-new-2-Q26 The instruction was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed least the reported “as much as $125 billion” in residual-value support (e5028) because it is described as possible, not as a confirmed obligation outstanding by FY2027 year-end. I also set aside Morgan Stanley’s estimate that potential credit exposure could reach $200 billion by 2028 (e3127): it concerns broader exposure and a later date, so it does not directly quantify this question’s year-end amount.\nT-new-2-Q27 The instruction most directly leading to rung 3 was: “Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.”\n\nI weighed least the report that the administration was “considering new tariffs”: it is an unnamed report without a decision, date, or scope. I also did not treat the White House official’s statement that reporting should be regarded as “baseless speculation” unless officially announced as a formal abandonment; it casts doubt on the report, but does not rule out the tariff initiative.\nT-new-2-Q31 The instruction I should have followed was: **“Do not add to or subtract from the previous score.”** I incorrectly moved the thesis from rung 2 to rung 1 without new evidence warranting a lower rung.\n\nI weighed these statements least:\n\n1. NVIDIA’s “up to 2 gigawatts” target (e4318): it is the reference, not proof that 2 GW is deployed or bindingly contracted.\n2. Firmus’s $2 billion equity round to accelerate Project Southgate (e1708): it gives no capacity, allocation, or timeline, so it cannot be translated into eligible GW by the deadline.\nT-new-2-Q4 The governing sentence was: “The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.”\n\nI weighed these two statements least as evidence of a *qualifying announcement*:\n\n- **e1450:** Commerce is “formally investigating” whether Chinese firms are accessing advanced U.S. chips. This raises the chance of action, but does not itself announce a new restriction or enforcement action explicitly tied to DeepSeek or third-country diversion.\n- **e968:** White House official Michael Kratsios accused Moonshot of accessing GB300 servers in Thailand. It is a specific allegation, but not a Commerce/BIS action or a confirmed finding.\nT-new-2-Q5 The instruction most directly supporting the rung was: “third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party).”\n\nI weighed NVIDIA’s “Our roadmap is intact” (e100) least because it gives no Kyber shipment date and does not explicitly rebut the reported delay. I also set aside “Vera Rubin is already in production” (e583) as weak evidence for this question: it concerns Rubin generally, not confirmation of Kyber NVL144 commercial shipments.\nT-new-3-Q23 “Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed **e2230** least: its 10 GW power plan and $4.2 billion grid investment are not evidence of FERC’s disposition or timing. I also set aside **e5215**: the CEO’s roughly 100 GW flexibility estimate is not a FERC schedule or decision, so it does little to distinguish “final disposition by year-end 2027” from “still open.”\nT-new-3-Q26 The instruction was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed least e2470’s “roughly $27bn” aggregate because the disclosed deal components give a more specific accounting basis for the total. I set aside e4851’s report that Poolside’s $1bn financing was part of NVIDIA’s led/co-led rounds because it explicitly does not say how much NVIDIA contributed; it does not establish any amount beyond the separately disclosed $1bn investment.\nT-new-3-Q4 The instruction most directly leading to rung 2 was: “Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it.”\n\nI weighed least NVIDIA’s statement that “Vera Rubin will scale up to a larger NVL576 domain in its planned 2027 timeline” (e263), because it concerns NVL576, not Kyber NVL144. I also treated “Vera Rubin, now in full production” with racks running at named partners (e2863) as counterevidence, not confirmation of Kyber-based Rubin Ultra commercial shipments. Rung 2 is my forecast of a standing deferral by the due date, not a claim that a formal deferral is already established.\nT-old-1-Q28 The instruction was: “Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. … compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed least e4974’s attribution of NVIDIA’s $1.3 billion of led or co-led round value to Poolside and Volta: those are total round values, not NVIDIA’s investment amounts. I also discounted e4916’s “up to $10 billion” Anthropic investment because it describes reported talks, not a completed or sized commitment.\nT-old-1-Q45 The instruction that led to rung 1 was: “third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts.”\n\nI weighed least:\n\n- “Anthropic is considering raising as much as $100 billion at a valuation of around $2 trillion.” It describes the possible IPO’s scale, not whether NVIDIA will invest.\n- “Anthropic is negotiating to secure NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA) as an anchor investor…” I treated this as the same investment report as e4916/e4946, not an independent new development; the evidence itself says the matcher considered those reports the same claim.\nT-old-1-Q7 “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed e5167 least because its opinion concerns Anthropic, OpenAI, and SpaceX—not the four hyperscalers in this question. I also set aside e5146’s $3–$4 trillion figure because it is an AI-capex target for 2030, not a 2027 estimate for these four companies.\nT-old-2-Q16 The instruction most directly behind the rung was: “Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat.”\n\nI weighed these statements least:\n\n- NVIDIA’s estimate of “demand for approximately $20 billion in total server CPUs” (e2544): it describes total market demand, not a cap on NVIDIA’s revenue.\n- AMD’s reported performance advantages over Vera (e5047–e5054): they suggest competitive risk, but do not quantify lost NVIDIA sales or revise its FY2027 revenue outlook.\nT-old-2-Q29 The key instruction was: “Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it.”\n\nI weighed least:\n\n- e2889: NVIDIA’s $18 billion commitment for the rest of its fiscal year is already included in the $43 billion base, so it adds no separate amount beyond that calculation.\n- e4729: The more than $42 billion of equity stakes purchased in the first half is reported spending, not a separate outstanding commitment balance; adding it would risk double counting rather than establish a higher commitments figure.\nT-old-2-Q6 The instruction was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed e4988 least: “could reach $1.5 trillion” is a conditional, broad AI-infrastructure figure, not a specific forecast for these four hyperscalers’ 2027 CapEx. I also gave little additional weight to e4781’s $1.3 trillion estimate because it repeats the same top-five estimate rather than adding independent evidence; the four-company outcome still requires applying a share proxy.\nT-old-2-Q9 The instruction most directly leading to the rung was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed e2572 least: its supply figure concerns FY2028 growth, so it does not directly quantify FY2027 revenue. I also discounted e2510, AWS’s 2-million-GPU deployment plan, because it spans 2027–2028 and does not specify the amount of FY2027 NVIDIA revenue. My prior answer’s $410 billion estimate was not adequately supported; I inferred a Q4 figure without enough evidence to justify it.\nT-old-3-Q14 The sentence that most directly led to the rung was: “reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat.”\n\nI weighed **e1030** least: AMD’s claimed 20% SPEC advantage is specific, but it does not quantify its effect on NVIDIA’s FY2027 CPU revenue. I also set aside **e1075**: it says some companies are designing their own data-center CPUs, but names no customers or gives no indication of lost NVIDIA demand. Neither changes the revenue estimate enough to move it below the rung-1 boundary.\nT-old-3-Q23 The instruction most directly driving rung 1 was: “third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts.”\n\nI weighed least e1381, which says the talks are early-stage and could collapse: it is a meaningful risk, but the specific financing discussions and time remaining still made signing more likely than not. I also weighed e4895 least: Huang’s “never a commitment” statement concerns the $100 billion pledge, not the separately reported chip-purchase financing talks, so I treated it as only a limited counterweight.\nT-old-3-Q3 The instruction most directly leading to rung 1 was: “reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat.” I applied that to first-half revenue, Q3 guidance, and the assumed Q4 sequential growth, then added the SemiAnalysis uplift.\n\nI weighed these two statements least:\n\n- NVIDIA’s “70% revenue growth for the coming year” (e4510): taken literally against FY2026 revenue, it implies about $367 billion, but it conflicts with the stronger near-term run-rate and guidance.\n- Analysts’ expected 90% Q3 and 65% Q4 growth (e5192): these are third-party forecasts, so I gave them less weight than company guidance. They were a counter-signal, not proof of lower revenue.\nT-old-3-Q33 The instruction was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed these two statements least:\n\n- **e2248:** BofA’s estimate of about $70 billion in equity investments. It gives no period and does not say that amount remains outstanding or committed at FY2027 filing.\n- **e5048:** More than $42 billion spent on equity stakes in the first half of FY2027. Spending is not the same as outstanding commitments, so it does not directly add to the $25 billion reported commitment balance.\nT-old-3-Q37 The instruction was: **“The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.”**\n\nI weighed least the estimate that HBM is 30%–40% of an accelerator’s build cost (e3378): it is a broad third-party estimate and does not quantify NVIDIA’s FY2028 margin impact. I also gave limited weight to SK Hynix’s estimate that memory demand could exceed supply beyond 2030 (e5183): it points to persistent pressure, but that horizon is later than FY2028 and provides no quantified cost effect.\nT-old-3-Q41 The instruction was: “A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand.”\n\nI weighed these statements least:\n\n- AMD’s estimate that the server CPU market could reach $220 billion (e4687): it describes the total market, not NVIDIA’s share or Vera revenue.\n- NVIDIA’s statement that Anthropic is evaluating Vera (e5044): an evaluation is not a purchase commitment, and no revenue or volume is specified.\nT-old-3-Q7 The sentence was: “State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.”\n\nI weighed e5293 least: the $156 billion concerns projects stalled or halted in 2025, not a quantified reduction to these four companies’ 2027 spending. I also weighed e5292 lightly: the ten-year grid-connection claim signals a constraint, but does not quantify how much 2027 capex it would defer.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md; for arm in J2a J2b; do diff -u src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/$arm.txt; cat docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/$arm.order.json; done; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md; for arm in J2a J2b; do diff -u src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/$arm.txt; cat docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/$arm.order.json; done; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# J2: the judge's next version, design for the council (2026-11-20, phase 1 steps 2–4)\n     2\t\n     3\t## What the census and the traces show\n     4\t- **The target.** 24 answers rejected by both readers (`census/CENSUS.md`). In about 16 of them the answer leaves the rung of its own\n     5\t  reference on a weak step. Main classes:\n     6\t  - O: overlapping amounts added (6);\n     7\t  - S: a figure of another scope taken as the value (6);\n     8\t  - E: an adjustment with no basis (5).\n     9\t- **The order of the answer (found at $0, decisive).**\n    10\t  - In all 48 stored answers of the probe set, the judge writes the fields in this order: `rung > reasons > cites > cites_views >\n    11\t    pushes > changed > why_changed > theme_pushes > reference > implied_outcome`. It chooses the rung first, and states the reference and\n    12\t    its own derivation last.\n    13\t  - The cause is code. `judging.schema_for` inserts `reference` and `implied_outcome` after `rung` in `required`. Its comment reads\n    14\t    \"after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\". But it appends them to the end of `properties`,\n    15\t    and the model writes the fields in `properties` order.\n    16\t  - So D260's design, \"the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\", never ran. The reader brief's order of\n    17\t    work (first the reference, then what the evidence implies, then the comparison) is reversed.\n    18\t  - This fits 7 of the 24 answers, whose arithmetic lands just across a boundary. It also fits the readers' recurring note that the\n    19\t    reasons justify a rung already chosen.\n    20\t- **The model's own account** (`poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/account/`, 24 continued conversations, $0.027). It names:\n    21\t  - \"State the implied figure … compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one\" (9);\n    22\t  - \"carries the guided growth forward\" (6);\n    23\t  - \"rumour … in proportion to their specificity\" (3);\n    24\t  - \"The rung is your forecast\" (3);\n    25\t  - \"discounted by default\" (1);\n    26\t  - \"Missing confirmation alone…\" (1).\n    27\t\n    28\t  Two answers concede the error: old-2 Q9 says \"I inferred a Q4 figure without enough evidence\"; new-2 Q31 says \"moved … without new\n    29\t  evidence\".\n    30\t- **Re-send noise.** The 48 stored requests are re-sent 3 times unchanged (arm v7, running). A target that flips on the re-send alone\n    31\t  is sampler noise and is reported apart.\n    32\t\n    33\t## Prompt audit (judging-v7 against the judgement ruler's reader brief and D260/D263)\n    34\t| Failure class | Request sentence that produces it | The standard's line | Verdict |\n    35\t|---|---|---|---|\n    36\t| Rung chosen before the derivation (all classes) | The schema's field order: rung first, `reference` and `implied_outcome` last. Sentence 10 lists the rung first | Reader brief: \"first establish what the market expected … then ask what the evidence implies, then compare the two\". D260: \"the answer states the reference and the implied outcome\", written before the reasons | **Contradiction (code)** |\n    37\t| O, overlapping amounts added | \"derive the outcome … check it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole …)\", applied only to dependencies, not to the judge's own sums | Reader brief and D260 (3): \"A part cannot exceed the whole it belongs to\"; \"the same claim … counts once\" | **Missing at its owner:** the identity is stated for dependencies, not for the judge's own arithmetic |\n    38\t| S, a figure of another scope as the value | \"a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share\", which covers periods and products, not companies, measures, or balance against flow | Ruler v1 §2′, the stage 3/4 analyst standard B: \"期间和定义要对上\" (period and definition must match). Extraction standard: a proxy of one aggregate is evidence for the same question, never its value | **Narrower than the standard** |\n    39\t| E, an adjustment with no basis | \"move when it crosses one\", together with \"once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay\" | Reader brief: \"a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it\"; \"Lean cautious, catch the increment\" | **Missing:** the shift is meant to be quantified, and the prompt never says that an unquantified adjustment does not cross |\n    40\t| W, talks taken as a likely completion (2) | \"third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity\" | Same line in the reader brief | **Misread**, 2 cases. Not targeted now |\n    41\t| R, a rung's own condition misapplied (2) | — | The rung text | **Misread**, 2 cases. Not targeted now |\n    42\t\n    43\t## The arms (one lever each; every sentence sourced)\n    44\t| Arm | Change | Source | Characters |\n    45\t|---|---|---|---|\n    46\t| v7 | None, re-sent as stored | Noise control | 4,924 |\n    47\t| **J2a** | Schema `properties` in the order `reference, implied_outcome, reasons, rung`, then the rest unchanged. Sentence 10 lists the fields in that order and says the rung \"follows from them\". Same fields and types; the code reads by name | D260 (its own written intent); the reader brief's order of work | 4,970 |\n    48\t| **J2b** | J2a, plus a closing check at the end of the system text: (1) overlap, (2) scope, (3) a step across a boundary names the item and the quantity that carry it, and an unquantified adjustment does not cross | (1) \"a part cannot exceed its whole\" (reader brief, D260); (2) analyst standard B and the extraction standard's proxy line; (3) the reader brief's \"quantified revision … shift it\" and \"Lean cautious\". The form is AGENTS §6: a test applied to each statement goes in a check at the end of the same prompt | 5,904. +934, reason: the closing-check form, with nothing cut, because each existing sentence carries a D260/D263 behaviour of the frozen gold |\n    49\t\n    50\t- **The examples in J2b's check** are generic accounting relations: a balance and its current portion, a total and a component, an uplift\n    51\t  on a base, a cost inside guidance. No company, product or number appears. The council is asked whether they are fitted to the bench.\n    52\t\n    53\t## The probe and the decision rule (written before any J2 send)\n    54\t- **Cases.** 24 targets, plus 24 controls that both readers supported, of the same draw and type (seeded). All 48 stored requests\n    55\t  rebuild byte for byte from code, the frozen system file and the stored user text; mutants (one character of system text, the effort)\n    56\t  fail the check.\n    57\t- **Sends.** Each arm × 48 cases × 3 repeats, at about $0.003 a call, about $0.45 an arm. Ledger `phase1.json`, $3.\n    58\t- **Reading.**\n    59\t  - Code first: the rung of every answer against the stored rung and the reference rung the answer names.\n    60\t  - Every answer whose rung differs from the stored one goes to the two blind readers (`mark_cards`: Codex with memories off, Claude).\n    61\t    It is mixed with the stored answers and the deck's plants under shuffled labels.\n    62\t  - So is a seeded sample of 8 same-rung answers per arm.\n    63\t  - Claude reads every changed answer beside its material.\n    64\t- **Pass, for J2 to go to the end-to-end slice:**\n    65\t  - at least 12 of the 24 targets supported by both readers in at least 2 of 3 repeats, against v7's re-send count on the same rule;\n    66\t  - no more than 2 of 24 controls lost (both readers rejecting in at least 2 of 3 repeats), and v7's re-send loses no more.\n    67\t- **Regression guard on the frozen ruler.**\n    68\t  - The judgement gold (gold-v1, sha `636c056d…`) on the stored r9-frozen-v108 draws: each judged seed question's last request at\n    69\t    2026-07-14, re-sent under v7 and the J2 arm that passes, 3 times each.\n    70\t  - Agreement with the gold must not fall below v7's re-sent agreement. That was 15/17, 15/17 and 16/17 as stored.\n    71\t- **Falsifiers.**\n    72\t  - J2a changes no more targets than v7's re-send: the order is not the mechanism. Then J2b's gain, if any, is attributed to the check\n    73\t    alone.\n    74\t  - J2b fixes targets but loses controls: the check over-corrects into the v5 stickiness that D260 removed. It stops there.\n    75\t\n    76\t## What this cannot show\n    77\t- **Opening, and the 17 matters never opened.** Phase 2.\n    78\t- **Effects across days.** A changed rung feeds the next day's previous conclusion. The end-to-end slice (plan step 7) shows those.\n    79\t- **A release verdict.** These cases are dev: they motivated the design. Acceptance is on a fresh window.\n    80\t\n    81\t## Out of scope for the council\n    82\tExtraction, opening, Steps 2–3, the frozen ruler's files, cost work.\n--- src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt\t2026-11-02 23:47:18\n+++ docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2a.txt\t2026-11-19 22:30:47\n@@ -7,5 +7,5 @@\n - “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n - A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n - Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n-- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n+- Return, in this order: reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); then the rung's one-based position, which follows from them; citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n - changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n[\"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"rung\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"]--- src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt\t2026-11-02 23:47:18\n+++ docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt\t2026-11-19 22:30:47\n@@ -7,5 +7,9 @@\n - “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n - A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n - Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n-- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n+- Return, in this order: reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); then the rung's one-based position, which follows from them; citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n - changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n+- Before you answer, check the implied outcome you derived, then correct it before choosing the rung:\n+  (1) Overlap: add two amounts only when neither contains the other. A balance and the part of it to be paid this year, a total and one of its components, an uplift on a base that already includes it, or a cost already inside guidance are not added.\n+  (2) Scope: each figure you use measures the question's own quantity: the same companies, measure, period and kind (a balance is not a flow; a cumulative amount is not an outstanding one). A figure for a wider or different scope is evidence about the question, used for what it shows, never taken as its value.\n+  (3) The step across a boundary: when your implied outcome sits in a different rung from the reference, name the evidence item and the quantity or fact in it that carries the outcome across that boundary. An adjustment that no item quantifies does not carry it across.\n[\"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"rung\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"]     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\n     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n     9\t- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n    10\t- Return, in this order: reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); then the rung's one-based position, which follows from them; citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n    11\t- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n    12\t- Before you answer, check the implied outcome you derived, then correct it before choosing the rung:\n    13\t  (1) Overlap: add two amounts only when neither contains the other. A balance and the part of it to be paid this year, a total and one of its components, an uplift on a base that already includes it, or a cost already inside guidance are not added.\n    14\t  (2) Scope: each figure you use measures the question's own quantity: the same companies, measure, period and kind (a balance is not a flow; a cumulative amount is not an outstanding one). A figure for a wider or different scope is evidence about the question, used for what it shows, never taken as its value.\n    15\t  (3) The step across a boundary: when your implied outcome sits in a different rung from the reference, name the evidence item and the quantity or fact in it that carries the outcome across that boundary. An adjustment that no item quantifies does not carry it across.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md; ls -la poc/data/e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03; rg --files poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md; ls -la poc/data/e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03; rg --files poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"Phase 1 of the hybrid plan (PLAN.md): the judge's stored final requests on the 24 answers both readers rejected, and matched\n     2\tcontrols both readers supported, re-sent with a judge variant.\n     3\t\n     4\t  python3 judge_probe.py cases                  # $0: cases.json (targets and matched controls, with their stored requests' ids)\n     5\t  python3 judge_probe.py check                  # $0: every stored request rebuilt byte for byte from code (schema) + system file + user\n     6\t  python3 judge_probe.py account <ledger>       # cents: the model's own account on the targets, continuing the stored conversation\n     7\t  python3 judge_probe.py probe <ledger> <arm> <repeats>   # cents: each case's request with the arm's system text, sent <repeats> times\n     8\t\n     9\tAn arm is a system-text file arms/<arm>.txt; arm 'v7' is the frozen judging-v7.txt itself (the control arm). The stored stores are read\n    10\tthrough read-only connections.\"\"\"\n    11\timport concurrent.futures\n    12\timport importlib.util\n    13\timport json\n    14\timport random\n    15\timport sqlite3\n    16\timport sys\n    17\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    18\t\n    19\tROOT = Path('/Users/lchingen/hivemind')\n    20\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    21\tsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n    22\tsys.path[:0] = [str(ROOT / 'src')]\n    23\tRUN = ROOT / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    24\tDIAG = ROOT / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic'\n    25\tKEYS = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/comparison-2026-11-17'\n    26\tOUT = ROOT / 'poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20'\n    27\tFROZEN_SYSTEM = ROOT / 'src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt'\n    28\tCONFIG = ROOT / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'\n    29\t# The 24 answers both readers rejected (census/CENSUS.md), by draw and deck label, with their census class.\n    30\tTARGETS = {\n    31\t    ('new-2', 'Q11'): 'E', ('new-2', 'Q20'): 'E', ('new-2', 'Q26'): 'S', ('new-2', 'Q27'): 'M', ('new-2', 'Q31'): 'S',\n    32\t    ('new-2', 'Q4'): 'M', ('new-2', 'Q5'): 'R', ('new-3', 'Q23'): 'M', ('new-3', 'Q26'): 'E', ('new-3', 'Q4'): 'R',\n    33\t    ('old-1', 'Q28'): 'S', ('old-1', 'Q45'): 'W', ('old-1', 'Q7'): 'S', ('old-2', 'Q16'): 'O', ('old-2', 'Q29'): 'O',\n    34\t    ('old-2', 'Q6'): 'S', ('old-2', 'Q9'): 'E', ('old-3', 'Q14'): 'O', ('old-3', 'Q23'): 'W', ('old-3', 'Q3'): 'O',\n    35\t    ('old-3', 'Q33'): 'O', ('old-3', 'Q37'): 'O', ('old-3', 'Q41'): 'E', ('old-3', 'Q7'): 'S',\n    36\t}\n    37\tSEED = 20261120\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\tdef load(name, path):\n    41\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)\n    42\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    43\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    44\t    return module\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef store_paths(draw):\n    48\t    \"\"\"(views, archive) of a finished comparison draw, as the comparison's mapping read them.\"\"\"\n    49\t    root = RUN / draw\n    50\t    record = json.loads((root / 'run.json').read_text())\n    51\t    if draw.startswith('new'):\n    52\t        judge = record['components']['judge']\n    53\t        inner = json.loads((root / judge['folder'] / 'run.json').read_text())[draw]\n    54\t        folder = root / judge['folder'] / inner['attempts'][-1]['folder']\n    55\t    else:\n    56\t        folder = root / record['components']['prod']['folder']\n    57\t    return folder / 'views.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite'\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef readonly(path):\n    61\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    62\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    63\t    return conn\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\tdef cases():\n    67\t    \"\"\"Targets, and per target one control from the same draw and of the same type that both readers marked worth tracking and\n    68\t    supported (seeded choice, no control used twice).\"\"\"\n    69\t    readings = json.loads((DIAG / 'deck/readings.json').read_text())['cards']\n    70\t    library_of = json.loads((KEYS / 'mapping-key-diagnostic.json').read_text())\n    71\t    deck_key = json.loads((KEYS / 'deck-key.json').read_text())\n    72\t    card_of = {(v['draw'], v['question']): c for c, v in deck_key.items() if v.get('role') == 'product'}\n    73\t    rng = random.Random(SEED)\n    74\t    out, used = [], set()\n    75\t    for (draw, label), census_class in sorted(TARGETS.items()):\n    76\t        library = {e['question_id']: e for e in json.loads((DIAG / f'mapping-out/library-{library_of[draw]}.json').read_text())}\n    77\t        mark = readings[draw][label]\n    78\t        assert mark['worth'] == 'worth' and mark['answer'] != 'supported', (draw, label, mark)\n    79\t        out.append({'case': f'T-{draw}-{label}', 'role': 'target', 'draw': draw, 'label': label, 'view_id': library[label]['source_id'],\n    80\t                    'type': mark['type'], 'class': census_class, 'card': card_of[(draw, label)], 'mark': mark['answer']})\n    81\t        pool = sorted(q for q, m in readings[draw].items()\n    82\t                      if m['worth'] == 'worth' and m['answer'] == 'supported' and m['type'] == mark['type'] and (draw, q) not in used\n    83\t                      and (draw, q) not in TARGETS and (draw, q) in card_of)\n    84\t        pick = rng.choice(pool)\n    85\t        used.add((draw, pick))\n    86\t        out.append({'case': f'C-{draw}-{pick}', 'role': 'control', 'draw': draw, 'label': pick, 'view_id': library[pick]['source_id'],\n    87\t                    'type': mark['type'], 'class': None, 'card': card_of[(draw, pick)], 'mark': 'supported'})\n    88\t    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    89\t    (OUT / 'cases.json').write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1))\n    90\t    print(len(out), 'cases:', sum(c['role'] == 'target' for c in out), 'targets,', sum(c['role'] == 'control' for c in out), 'controls')\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\tdef stored(case):\n    94\t    \"\"\"The latest stored judgement of the case's view and its archived request and answer.\"\"\"\n    95\t    views, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\n    96\t    v = readonly(views)\n    97\t    j = v.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc limit 1', (case['view_id'],)).fetchone()\n    98\t    a = readonly(archive)\n    99\t    row = a.execute('select request_json, response_json, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1', (j['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()\n   100\t    return dict(j), json.loads(row['request_json']), json.loads(row['response_json']), json.loads(row['answer_json'])\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef rebuild(stored_request, system_text, order=None):\n   104\t    \"\"\"The request as production builds it (model.build_request, key order and schema from code), with the given system text. With\n   105\t    `order`, the schema's properties are written in that order (the same fields and types; the model writes fields in this order).\"\"\"\n   106\t    from hivemind import config, model\n   107\t    from hivemind.views import judging\n   108\t    cfg = config.load(CONFIG)\n   109\t    user = stored_request['messages'][1]['content']\n   110\t    schema = judging.schema_for(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version)\n   111\t    if order is not None:\n   112\t        assert sorted(order) == sorted(schema['properties']), 'an order names exactly the schema fields'\n   113\t        schema['properties'] = {field: schema['properties'][field] for field in order}\n   114\t    return model.build_request(cfg.rejudging, system_text, user, schema, 'judgement', cfg.provider)\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\tdef arm_spec(arm):\n   118\t    \"\"\"(system text, schema order or None) of an arm; 'v7' is the frozen judge as stored.\"\"\"\n   119\t    if arm == 'v7':\n   120\t        return FROZEN_SYSTEM.read_text(encoding='utf-8'), None\n   121\t    order_file = HERE / 'arms' / f'{arm}.order.json'\n   122\t    return (HERE / 'arms' / f'{arm}.txt').read_text(encoding='utf-8'), (json.loads(order_file.read_text()) if order_file.exists() else None)\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\tdef check():\n   126\t    \"\"\"$0: each stored request, rebuilt from the frozen system file, code's schema and the stored user text, has the stored sha.\"\"\"\n   127\t    from hivemind import model\n   128\t    frozen = FROZEN_SYSTEM.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n   129\t    rows = json.loads((OUT / 'cases.json').read_text())\n   130\t    bad = []\n   131\t    for case in rows:\n   132\t        judgement, request, _, _ = stored(case)\n   133\t        _, sha = model.request_identity(rebuild(request, frozen))\n   134\t        if sha != judgement['request_sha256']:\n   135\t            bad.append(case['case'])\n   136\t    print(f'{len(rows) - len(bad)} of {len(rows)} stored requests rebuilt byte for byte', 'mismatch: ' + ', '.join(bad) if bad else '')\n   137\t    if bad:\n   138\t        raise SystemExit(1)\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\tdef transport_for(ledger_path):\n   142\t    budget_replay = load('budget_replay', ROOT / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   143\t    ledger = budget_replay.SharedLedger(ledger_path)\n   144\t    return budget_replay.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\tACCOUNT_QUESTION = ('Look back at the answer you just gave. Which sentence of your instructions led you to this rung? Quote it. Which two '\n   148\t                    'statements in the evidence did you set aside or weigh least, and why? Answer in under 150 words.')\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef account(ledger_path):\n   152\t    \"\"\"Cents: the stored conversation of each target, continued with one question; plain text, no schema.\"\"\"\n   153\t    transport, ledger = transport_for(ledger_path)\n   154\t    rows = [c for c in json.loads((OUT / 'cases.json').read_text()) if c['role'] == 'target']\n   155\t    folder = OUT / 'account'\n   156\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   157\t\n   158\t    def one(case):\n   159\t        _, request, response, _ = stored(case)\n   160\t        follow = {'model': request['model'],\n   161\t                  'messages': request['messages'] + [{'role': 'assistant', 'content': response['choices'][0]['message']['content']},\n   162\t                                                     {'role': 'user', 'content': ACCOUNT_QUESTION}],\n   163\t                  'max_completion_tokens': 4000, 'reasoning_effort': request.get('reasoning_effort', 'medium')}\n   164\t        answer = transport('openai', follow)\n   165\t        text = answer['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   166\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case, 'question': ACCOUNT_QUESTION, 'account': text,\n   167\t                                                                'usage': answer.get('usage')}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   168\t        return case['case']\n   169\t\n   170\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(8) as pool:\n   171\t        for name in pool.map(one, rows):\n   172\t            print('account', name, flush=True)\n   173\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\tdef probe(ledger_path, arm, repeats):\n   177\t    \"\"\"Cents: each case's rebuilt request with the arm's system text, sent `repeats` times, each answer stored with its usage.\"\"\"\n   178\t    transport, ledger = transport_for(ledger_path)\n   179\t    system, order = arm_spec(arm)\n   180\t    rows = json.loads((OUT / 'cases.json').read_text())\n   181\t    folder = OUT / 'probe' / arm\n   182\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   183\t    jobs = [(case, k) for case in rows for k in range(1, repeats + 1)]\n   184\t\n   185\t    def one(job):\n   186\t        case, k = job\n   187\t        _, request, _, _ = stored(case)\n   188\t        response = transport('openai', rebuild(request, system, order))\n   189\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   190\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case, 'repeat': k, 'arm': arm, 'answer': json.loads(content),\n   191\t                                                                    'usage': response.get('usage')}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   192\t        return f\"{case['case']}-{k}\"\n   193\t\n   194\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(8) as pool:\n   195\t        for name in pool.map(one, jobs):\n   196\t            print('probe', name, flush=True)\n   197\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   201\t    command = sys.argv[1]\n   202\t    if command == 'cases':\n   203\t        cases()\n   204\t    elif command == 'check':\n   205\t        check()\n   206\t    elif command == 'account':\n   207\t        account(sys.argv[2])\n   208\t    elif command == 'probe':\n   209\t        probe(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], int(sys.argv[4]))\n   210\t    else:\n   211\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n     1\t# Hybrid system: build and test plan (2026-11-20, D681)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Alex, 2026-11-20:** \"可以啊，你现在开始做hybrid system 的构建和测试，不要犯了和做新系统一样的错误到最后才发现问题\". This was his reply to\n     4\tthe proposal to fix, first, the old system's judge reasoning errors as a new judge version: a council review first, then a test of a few\n     5\tcents (`docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md`, \"Where the old system loses\").\n     6\t\n     7\t## The new system's mistakes, and the guard for each\n     8\t| Mistake | Where it showed | Guard in this plan |\n     9\t|---|---|---|\n    10\t| Steps were tuned on their own scores. The hand-off broke and was found at the end: Step 1's questions refused by the ladder, 19–27 of 60 (D432) | the release comparison, D676 | Every change is accepted only by its effect on final answers, read by blind readers on the analyst matter list. An end-to-end slice runs in week 1, not at the end |\n    11\t| The attainable verdict was not computed: $145 spent on a knowable result | D676 | The ceilings are below, computed before any send |\n    12\t| A policy removed matters by construction (company figures, D382), and it was known only at the end | D676 | Alex decides the figure questions for the hybrid now (below) |\n    13\t| Lines with no source, or that the change could not move (the merge test's P2) | D680 | Every line names its source and the change that can move it |\n    14\t| Choices made on the test set, and fix-and-rerun loops | council-loop traps | Designed on the stored failures of 09-07..09-20 (dev). Accepted once on a window the design never saw, with its matter list built blind before any hybrid output is read |\n    15\t\n    16\t## What the hybrid is\n    17\t| Piece | From | Status |\n    18\t|---|---|---|\n    19\t| Opening questions and their answer choices | Old (poc-v118) | Unchanged |\n    20\t| Reading articles | Old extraction (control arm) or clean Step 1 c8 (hybrid arm) | c8's effect on final answers is measured end to end, not assumed. On the 32 matters, old's losses are not reading losses |\n    21\t| Judging | Frozen judging-v7, then a new version (J2) | The change; Alex opened it on 2026-11-20 |\n    22\t| Clean Steps 2–3 | Not in the first build | Added only if a measured loss calls for them |\n    23\t\n    24\t## Attainable, on the frozen 32 matters (from the stored readings, $0)\n    25\t- **Old serves 10.**\n    26\t- **The judge fix can add M08 and M14.** Old opened each in 3 of 3 draws, and the readers rejected every answer for reasoning:\n    27\t  - adding amounts that overlap;\n    28\t  - a cumulative estimate taken for an outstanding balance;\n    29\t  - a five-company or company-forecast figure taken for a four-company answer.\n    30\t- **M30 (+1)** only if company figures are kept.\n    31\t- **M05, M09 and M25** (served in 1 of 3 draws) and the **17 never opened** move only with opening, not the judge.\n    32\t- **The release lead** (D665: a − b ≥ 5 and a ≥ 2b against old) is out of reach for the judge fix alone, with a ≤ 3. The judge fix is a\n    33\t  quality gain. A release needs phase 2, opening.\n    34\t- **If D382 applies to the hybrid** (no company-figure questions), old keeps 5–6 matters the hybrid cannot serve, and the hybrid loses by\n    35\t  construction. Hence Alex's decision now.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Phase 1: the judge (J2)\n    38\t1. **$0 census.** Every answer of the 5 stored draws that the readers rejected or split, among the questions rated worth tracking. The\n    39\t   same frozen judge answered old-1..3 and new-2..3. Each is classified by mechanism, from the readers' reasons and the judge's own:\n    40\t   - overlap or arithmetic;\n    41\t   - range against the answer's own estimate;\n    42\t   - scope (other companies, year or measure);\n    43\t   - source weight (a company's own forecast over independent ones);\n    44\t   - missing material;\n    45\t   - the boundary between two ranges;\n    46\t   - other.\n    47\t\n    48\t   The largest class is the target.\n    49\t2. **Mechanism.** The whole judge request is read for 10 cases. The model's own account is taken on up to 10, at a cent each.\n    50\t3. **Design.** A prompt audit of judging-v7 against the judgement ruler (`ruler-v1.md`) and the standards. The levers are structural\n    51\t   first, for example a required estimate field whose chosen range code checks. Every sentence names its source, or goes to Alex.\n    52\t4. **Council A** on the design: an independent Codex read, then challenge rounds to consensus.\n    53\t5. **$0 checks.**\n    54\t   - Stored requests are rebuilt byte for byte.\n    55\t   - A synthetic answer passes every code check.\n    56\t   - J2 sits beside judging-v7. The production default and the frozen tests stay unchanged, apart from the code that admits a second\n    57\t     version.\n    58\t6. **A probe of cents.**\n    59\t   - The stored final requests of the failing cases are re-sent with J2, 3 times each.\n    60\t   - As many supported answers are re-sent as controls, which must not regress.\n    61\t   - Blind readers mark them, mixed with the archived answers.\n    62\t   - **Pass:** at least half the failing cases flip to supported, with no control lost.\n    63\t7. **End-to-end slice in week 1.**\n    64\t   - The merge-test harness (the 09-06 copy) is extended to every open question.\n    65\t   - It runs 09-07..09-20 on two old draws, with J2, in both reading arms.\n    66\t   - Readers mark every answer, and the 32 matters are counted as dev, since they are exposed.\n    67\t   - The cost is estimated from archived tokens before the send.\n    68\t8. **Acceptance** on a fresh window, run once on Alex's word.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Phase 2: opening\n    71\t- A census of why the 17 matters were never opened, after phase 1's end-to-end slice. It is not designed now.\n    72\t\n    73\t## Limits\n    74\t- The frozen ruler is unchanged.\n    75\t- No paid send before the council and the $0 checks.\n    76\t- Phase 1 through step 6 costs about $1. Step 7's estimate is written before it runs.\n    77\t- Nothing is pushed or deployed.\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x@   8 lchingen  staff   256 Nov  3 01:14 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 229 lchingen  staff  7328 Nov 19 22:28 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 lchingen  staff   288 Nov  3 01:03 d1\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 lchingen  staff   288 Nov  3 01:08 d2\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 lchingen  staff   288 Nov  3 01:04 d3\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   134 Nov  3 00:12 r9-frozen-v108-d1.launch.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   134 Nov  3 00:12 r9-frozen-v108-d2.launch.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   134 Nov  3 00:12 r9-frozen-v108-d3.launch.log\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2a.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2b.order.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/arms/J2a.order.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/rejected-answers.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-a-codex.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-a-codex.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-a-brief.md\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q26-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q6-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q1-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q23-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q23-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q6-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q4-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q31-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q26-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q25-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q27-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q11-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q20-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q20-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q14-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q25-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q18-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q14-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/C-new-2-Q18-2.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q20-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q11-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q27-3.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q5-1.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/probe/v7/T-new-2-Q27-2.json\npoc/data/hy