es                                       Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese\nq09 agree         2.5e+10..6e+10              v9 rung 4 Bearish 20000000000.0..400000 no      no      What total amount of financing commitments and capacity back\nq10 no judgement  {'text': 'Gross margin holds about 75% through Q2 (i281, i153) and I expect 74-76% for the year (q03). Revenue grew 85% while net income grew 211% (i302), showing operating leverage, and revenue approaches $100bn a quarter with accelerating growth (i295); a non-GAAP figure adds back stock compensation. I bet 65-69%.', 'low': 65, 'high': 69, 'yes_no': None, 'items': ['i163', 'i281', 'i302', 'i295']}v10 never judged                                        What non-GAAP operating margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027\nq11 agree         9..10                       v11 rung 1 Strongly bul 10.0..inf       no      no      What non-GAAP diluted earnings per share will NVIDIA report \nq12 no judgement  {'text': \"NVIDIA's cash goes into other things than its own plant: $5bn into Intel (i007), stakes in Verkada and Gradium (i001, i285), $3.5bn of lease guarantees (i006), the backstop programme (i120), an $80bn buyback (i301) and a debt raise of at least $20bn (i052); the Valar Atomics AI factory is exploration only (i145). Capital spending should still grow with a company approaching $100bn quarters (i295). I bet $7-11bn.\", 'low': 7000000000, 'high': 11000000000, 'yes_no': None, 'items': ['i131', 'i007', 'i006', 'i145', 'i295']}v12 never judged                                        How much will NVIDIA spend on capital expenditures in FY2027\nq13 agree         8.5e+11..1.05e+12           v13 rung 5 $1000 billio 1000000000000.0 yes             How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-cent\nq14 no_view                                                                                           What CoWoS advanced-packaging capacity will TSMC reach by th\nq15 no_view                     