{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,re; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; cs=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text());\nfor c in cs:\n if c[\\\"case\\\"] in {\\\"T-old-2-Q29\\\",\\\"T-old-3-Q7\\\"}:\n  j,r,b,a=p.stored(c); print(c[\\\"case\\\"]); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(l for l in r[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"].splitlines() if l.startswith(\\\"- \\\") and re.search(r\\\"\\\\\"'$25 billion|'\"\\\\\"'$18 billion|'\"\\\\\"'$1.08 trillion|'\"\\\\\"'$1.3 trillion\", l))[:3800])'\"'\nrg -n 'def retire|def lookup' src/hivemind/archive.py; nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '262,306p'; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"T-old-2-Q29\n- e2620 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of 2026-07-26.\n- e2889 [party_statement; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's statement; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said on Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the remainder of its fiscal year, in addition to $47.9 billion held in private companies.\n- e3917 [fact; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's latest earnings report; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6d453f248e1068162655b045 2026-09-04] NVIDIA reported $25 billion in equity investment commitments as of July 26.\n- e4053 [fact; calcalistech.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] NVIDIA reported about $99 billion invested in other companies’ shares and a further $25 billion of future investment commitments at FY2027 Q2 quarter-end.\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2028-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 4 $1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is approximately $1.08 trillion for calendar 2027, which is rung 3. The implied estimate remains about $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate four-to-five share proxy (about $730 billion of $800 billion) to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five est\nT-old-3-Q7\n- e2080 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:1219126db2e6631aa1264142 2026-08-16] Bank of America said analyst consensus for hyperscaler capital spending in calendar 2027 rose from $480 billion in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion in August 2026, up about 127%.\n- e2759 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said the five largest hyperscalers’ capital expenditures are expected to total nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\n- e4513 [party_statement; Jon Quast; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:b851795e16e32bc54280459b 2026-09-08] Jon Quast said NVIDIA expected the hyperscalers to spend $1.3 trillion on capex in the coming year, $500 billion more than their spending that year.\n- e5056 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source BofA Global Research ; from gnews:ca2f580191a4509ac38bc1cf 2026-09-15] BofA Global Research estimated that Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta and Oracle could spend $1.08 trillion collectively on capital expenditures in calendar 2027, about 36% more than in 2026.\n- e5081 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d 2026-09-15] NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\n- e5105 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8cdef40aebf24cdc89f530ff 2026-09-16] NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers’ annual capital spending is on track to reach $800 billion in 2026 and is expected to reach $1.3 trillion in 2027.\n- e5115 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management pegged top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures at $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\n- e5185 [third_party_view; fool.com author Harsh Chauhan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4fbadb3b4cb5846297a34b0a 2026-09-16] NVIDIA estimates the top five hyperscalers' capex could reach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, up from $800 billion in calendar 2026.\n- e5359 [party_statement; fool.com (Harsh Chauhan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA projected that the five largest U.S. hyperscalers’ capital expenditure would reach $1.3 trillion in 2027.\n- e5377 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4ee5d8f73b7bcfc2f2111ad1 2026-09-19] The forecast for data-center capital expenditures by the five largest AI hyperscalers rises to $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\nrg: src/hivemind/archive.py: IO error for operation on src/hivemind/archive.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   296\t            raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   297\t        try:\n   298\t            response = jev.transport(request)\n   299\t        except Exception:\n   300\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate, kind='jev')\n   301\t            raise\n   302\t        usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   303\t        tokens = usage.get('input_tokens') if isinstance(usage, dict) else None\n   304\t        if isinstance(tokens, int) and not isinstance(tokens, bool) and tokens > 0:\n   305\t            # an unanswered attempt inside jev.transport was the same request, so each of the three is billed at most this input;\n   306\t            # the whole charge is settled, so a charge above the reservation sets the overrun flag\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-8cteqPVt' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-19 22:33:48.243 xcodebuild[63820:63021916]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-19 22:33:48.439 xcodebuild[63820:63021915] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-WDOZjHKF' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-19 22:33:48.814 xcodebuild[63826:63021932]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-19 22:33:48.927 xcodebuild[63826:63021931] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n M docs/DECISIONS-log.md\n M docs/DECISIONS.md\n M docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md\n?? docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; cases=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text()); rungs={c[\\\"case\\\"]:p.stored(c)[0][\\\"rung\\\"] for c in cases}; out=collections.defaultdict(list);\nfor f in (p.OUT/\\\"probe/v7\\\").glob(\\\"*.json\\\"):\n try: d=json.loads(f.read_text())\n except json.JSONDecodeError: continue\n name=d[\\\"case\\\"][\\\"case\\\"]; out[name].append(d[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"rung\\\"]\"'!=rungs[name]);\nfor role in \"TC\":\n aa=[r for n,r in out.items() if n.startswith(role)]; print(role,len(aa),sum(map(len,aa)),sum(map(sum,aa)),[n for n,r in out.items() if n.startswith(role) and sum(r)>=2])'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
